    "html": "<h2>August 28 Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 285)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the historical provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and pure narrative synopses for broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 28</strong> across American network radio, BBC Radio 4, and syndicated transcriptions, three Western adventures of <em>The Cisco Kid</em> (1952, 1956, 1958) starring Jack Mather, Harry Lang, and Mel Blanc, Chester Stratton in <em>Hop Harrigan</em>, Michael Hordern &amp; Richard Briers in P.G. Wodehouse&#39;s <em>Joy in the Morning</em>, and Bob Nolan with The Sons of the Pioneers on <em>The 10-2-4 Ranch</em> for Dr. Pepper (1945–1973):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 28 Archival Inventory (Increment 285)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Cisco_Kid_1952.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Dynamite on Right of Way</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Dynamite on the Right of Way&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Syndicated / Ziv</strong><br>1952-08-28</td>\n<td><strong>Regional Bakeries</strong><br>Weber&#39;s Bread / Tip-Top</td>\n<td><strong>Jack Mather</strong>, <strong>Harry Lang</strong></td>\n<td><strong>O. Henry</strong> (Creator)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Juvenile&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Americana&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Cisco and Pancho race against time to stop railroad saboteurs from detonating a dynamite charge under a passenger train trestle.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Cisco_Kid_1956.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Silver Lode Mystery</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Silver Lode Mystery&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Syndicated / Ziv</strong><br>1956-08-28</td>\n<td><strong>Commercial</strong><br>Regional Sponsors</td>\n<td><strong>Jack Mather</strong>, <strong>Mel Blanc</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Ziv Production Staff</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Juvenile&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Americana&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Cisco and Pancho protect a widowed prospector whose newly discovered silver vein attracts a ruthless gang of claim jumpers.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Cisco_Kid_1958.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>641 the Sheriff&#39;s 44&#39;s</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Sheriff&#39;s .44s (Episode 641)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Syndicated / Ziv</strong><br>1958-08-28</td>\n<td><strong>Commercial</strong><br>Regional Sponsors</td>\n<td><strong>Jack Mather</strong>, <strong>Mel Blanc</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Ziv Production Staff</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Juvenile&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Americana&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Cisco and Pancho investigate when a respected frontier town sheriff is framed for an armed bank robbery using his stolen custom revolvers.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Hop_Harrigan_1947.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Channel Wing Plane 02</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Channel Wing Plane (Part 2)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1947-08-28<br>5:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Aviation Serial</td>\n<td><strong>Chester Stratton</strong>, <strong>Glenn Riggs</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Jon Blummer</strong> (Creator)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Aviation&quot;, &quot;Juvenile&quot;, &quot;Serial&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Aviation hero Hop Harrigan and mechanic Tank Tinker test-fly a revolutionary prototype channel-wing aircraft while dodging foreign saboteurs.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>What_Ho_Jeeves_1973.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Episode 3 Of 8</code>, <code>Joy in Morning</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Joy in the Morning (Part 3)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>BBC Radio 4</strong><br>1973-08-28</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>BBC Comedy Drama</td>\n<td><strong>Michael Hordern</strong>, <strong>Richard Briers</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Chris Miller (Adapter)</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;British&quot;, &quot;Satire&quot;, &quot;Literary&quot;, &quot;Adaptation&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Bertie Wooster finds himself embroiled in romantic misunderstandings in Steeple Bumpleigh while Jeeves concocts a scheme to placate Lord Worplesdon.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>10-2-4_Ranch_1945.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Ten Two Four Time Rhythm Range</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Ten-Two-Four Time on the Rhythm Range&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Syndicated Elec</strong><br>1945-08-28</td>\n<td><strong>The Dr. Pepper Co.</strong><br>&quot;Drink a Bite to Eat&quot;</td>\n<td><strong>Sons of the Pioneers</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Bob Nolan</strong>, <strong>Pat Brady</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Country&quot;, &quot;Americana&quot;, &quot;Vocal&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Bob Nolan and The Sons of the Pioneers perform Western swing standards and four-part cowboy vocal harmonies from the Dr. Pepper ranch.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 28</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 28</strong>: 180</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
