    "html": "<h2>August 28 Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 274)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the historical provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and pure narrative synopses for broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 28</strong> across American network radio, three landmark <em>Meet the Press</em> interviews (1955 Soviet agriculture with Dr. W.V. Lambert, 1960 Eisenhower HEW Secretary Arthur Flemming, and 1966 AFL-CIO President George Meany), Irna Phillips&#39; <em>The Guiding Light</em> for Ivory Soap, Bob Trout &amp; William L. Shirer reporting on the Axis Vienna pact, and Kirk Douglas swashbuckling as Renaissance artist Benvenuto Cellini on <em>The Prudential Family Hour of Stars</em> (1940–1966):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 28 Archival Inventory (Increment 274)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Meet_Press_1955.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Dr. W V Lambert</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Dr. W.V. Lambert&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1955-08-28<br>6:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Public Affairs Interview</td>\n<td><strong>Ned Brooks</strong>, <strong>Lawrence Spivak</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Dr. W.V. Lambert</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;News&quot;, &quot;Interview&quot;, &quot;Public Affairs&quot;, &quot;Agriculture&quot;, &quot;Cold War&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Dr. W.V. Lambert faces press interrogation regarding Soviet agricultural conditions and collective farm productivity following a groundbreaking visit to the USSR.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Meet_Press_1960.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Arthur S Flemming</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Arthur S. Flemming&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1960-08-28<br>6:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Public Affairs Interview</td>\n<td><strong>Ned Brooks</strong>, <strong>Lawrence Spivak</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Arthur S. Flemming</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;News&quot;, &quot;Interview&quot;, &quot;Public Affairs&quot;, &quot;Politics&quot;, &quot;Government&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>HEW Secretary Arthur S. Flemming is questioned on medical care legislation for the elderly, federal school construction aid, and public health safeguards.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Meet_Press_1966.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>George Meary</code>, <code>George Meany</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;George Meany&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1966-08-28<br>12:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Public Affairs Interview</td>\n<td><strong>Edwin Newman</strong>, <strong>Lawrence Spivak</strong></td>\n<td><strong>George Meany</strong> (AFL-CIO)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;News&quot;, &quot;Interview&quot;, &quot;Public Affairs&quot;, &quot;Labor&quot;, &quot;Economics&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>AFL-CIO President George Meany defends organized labor&#39;s collective bargaining rights, airline strike settlements, and wage guideline resistance.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Guiding_Light_1950.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Meta Finds Allies</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Meta Finds Allies&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC)</strong><br>1950-08-28<br>1:45 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Procter &amp; Gamble</strong><br>Ivory Soap / Duz</td>\n<td><strong>Jone Allison</strong>, <strong>Lyle Sudrow</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Irna Phillips</strong> (Creator)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Soap Opera&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Family&quot;, &quot;Serial&quot;, &quot;Domestic&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Meta Bauer seeks support from family members as legal pressures mount regarding custody arrangements and her volatile marriage to Ted White.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>CBS_News_1940.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>CBS News Axis Foreign Ministers Meet</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Axis Foreign Ministers Meet&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC)</strong><br>1940-08-28<br>8:00 AM EDST</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Wartime News</td>\n<td><strong>Bob Trout</strong>, <strong>William L. Shirer</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Eric Sevareid</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;News&quot;, &quot;Broadcast Journalism&quot;, &quot;Wartime&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;World War II&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>CBS correspondents report on Axis foreign ministers meeting in Vienna to partition Romanian territory and the escalating London air raids.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Prudential_1949.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The Firebrand</code>, <code>Kirk Douglas</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Firebrand&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC)</strong><br>1949-08-28<br>6:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Prudential Co.</strong><br>&quot;Strength of Gibraltar&quot;</td>\n<td><strong>Kirk Douglas</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Carmen Dragon Orchestra</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Romance&quot;, &quot;Anthology&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Renaissance Florentine goldsmith and adventurer Benvenuto Cellini schemes his way out of prison and courts the Duchess of Florence.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 28</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 28</strong>: 114</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
