    "html": "<h2>August 27 Archival Enrichment (Increment 216)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the historical provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and pure narrative synopses for broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 27</strong> across American and British radio, three generations of young prodigies on <em>The Quiz Kids</em> for Alka-Seltzer (1941 literature/ornithology, 1944 Joel Kupperman wartime geography, 1950 Hiawatha &amp; astronomy), <em>The Comic Weekly Man</em> reading the Sunday funny papers for <em>Puck</em>, and two historic Anglo-American documentary collaborations on <em>Transatlantic Call</em> (Coventry reconstruction and Burl Ives singing the &quot;Song of America&quot;) (1941–1950):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 27 Archival Inventory (Increment 216)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Quiz_Kids_1941.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Child Prodigies 1941</code>, <code>Alka-Seltzer</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Child Prodigies of 1941&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Blue (WJZ)</strong><br>1941-08-27<br>8:00 PM EDST</td>\n<td><strong>Miles Laboratories</strong><br>Alka-Seltzer &amp; One-A-Day</td>\n<td><strong>Joe Kelly</strong> (Quizmaster), <strong>Gerard Darrow</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Joan Bishop</strong>, <strong>Richard Williams</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Quiz Show&quot;, &quot;Game Show&quot;, &quot;Educational&quot;, &quot;Children&quot;, &quot;Americana&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Quizmaster Joe Kelly tests young school prodigies on Shakespearean quotes, algebra equations, and ornithology facts sent in by listeners.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Quiz_Kids_1944.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Wartime Geography &amp; Science</code>, <code>Joel</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Wartime Geography &amp; Science Prodigies&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Blue (WJZ)</strong><br>1944-08-27<br>7:30 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Miles Laboratories</strong><br>Alka-Seltzer</td>\n<td><strong>Joe Kelly</strong> (Quizmaster), <strong>Joel Kupperman</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Harve Fischman</strong>, <strong>Ruthie Duskin</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Quiz Show&quot;, &quot;Game Show&quot;, &quot;Educational&quot;, &quot;Children&quot;, &quot;Americana&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Eight-year-old math wizard Joel Kupperman and fellow child prodigies solve rapid-fire mental arithmetic and identify Pacific islands on naval maps.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Quiz_Kids_1950.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Hiawatha And Mini Ha Ha</code>, <code>1950</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Hiawatha and Minnehaha&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1950-08-27<br>3:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Miles Laboratories</strong><br>Alka-Seltzer &amp; Bactine</td>\n<td><strong>Joe Kelly</strong> (Quizmaster), <strong>Joel Kupperman</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Naomi Cooks</strong>, <strong>Melvin Miles</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Quiz Show&quot;, &quot;Game Show&quot;, &quot;Educational&quot;, &quot;Children&quot;, &quot;Literature&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>The panel of gifted children answers questions on Longfellow&#39;s epic poetry, American folklore heroes, and classical astronomy constellations.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Comic_Weekly_1950.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Riddle about Chimney, Snookums</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Snookums &amp; Sunday Funnies&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>WOR / Synd</strong><br>1950-08-27<br>9:00 AM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Puck — Comic Weekly</strong><br>Hearst Sunday Papers</td>\n<td><strong>The Comic Weekly Man</strong> (Narrator)</td>\n<td><strong>George McManus</strong> (Comics)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Children&quot;, &quot;Comics&quot;, &quot;Americana&quot;, &quot;Humor&quot;, &quot;Storytelling&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>The Comic Weekly Man dramatically acts out voices and sound effects while reading the Sunday comic strips, including George McManus&#39;s &#39;The Newlyweds and Their Baby Snookums&#39;.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Transatlantic_Call_1944a.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Eye Witness 52</code>, <code>Coventry</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Eye Witness 52 (Coventry Rebuilding)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS / BBC</strong><br>1944-08-27<br>12:30 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Joint Wartime Series</td>\n<td><strong>BBC &amp; CBS Production Staff</strong></td>\n<td><strong>BBC / CBS Documentary Unit</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Documentary&quot;, &quot;Wartime&quot;, &quot;British&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Live Broadcast&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>A documentary broadcast chronicling the resilience of English factory workers and townspeople rebuilding industrial manufacturing plants in blitzed Coventry.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Transatlantic_Call_1944b.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Song Of America</code>, <code>Burl Ives</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Song of America (Folk Ballads &amp; Frontier Roots)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>BBC / CBS</strong><br>1944-08-27<br>1:00 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Cultural Exchange</td>\n<td><strong>Burl Ives</strong>, <strong>Alan Lomax</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS Symphony Orchestra</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Documentary&quot;, &quot;Folk Music&quot;, &quot;Americana&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Cultural&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Folksinger Burl Ives performs traditional American ballads and work songs, explaining the cultural history of Midwestern pioneers to British radio listeners.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 27</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 27</strong>: 209</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
