    "html": "<h2>August 26 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 165)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, serial multi-part narrative arcs, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 26</strong> across American and British radio, Elliott and Cathy Lewis starring in <em>The Prize Fighter</em> on <em>On Stage</em>, Conrad Nagel presenting the story of Father Flanagan&#39;s Boys Town on <em>Radio Reader&#39;s Digest</em> for Campbell&#39;s Soup, Antoinette Donnelly&#39;s flight on the double-decker Pan Am Boeing 377 Stratocruiser, Frank Lovejoy on <em>Men at Sea</em>, Bob Trout on <em>CBS News</em>, and <em>Retribution</em> (1940–1954):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 26 Archival Inventory (Increment 165)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Retribution_1947.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Retribution 1947-08-26</code>, <code>The Iron Master&#39;s Nemesis</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Iron Master&#39;s Nemesis (John Carson &amp; Ralph Michael — Retribution)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Syndicated</strong><br>1947-08-26<br>(Towers of London)</td>\n<td><strong>Local Merchants</strong><br>Moral Justice Anthology</td>\n<td><strong>John Carson</strong> (Narrator), <strong>Ralph Michael</strong></td>\n<td><strong>George Bellak</strong>, <strong>Harry Alan Towers</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Suspense&quot;, &quot;Psychological&quot;, &quot;Noir&quot;, &quot;British&quot;, &quot;Short Form&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Retribution! The inescapable law of nature that brings every crime to light and every evildoer to justice! In &#39;The Iron Master&#39;s Nemesis&#39;, a ruthless Sheffield foundry owner causes the fatal machinery accident of an inventor to steal his patent, only to be trapped in the automated foundry by the inventor&#39;s loyal apprentice.&quot;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Around_NY_1949.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Boeing Stratocruiser Flight</code>, <code>Antoinette Donnelly Stratocruiser</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Pan Am Boeing Stratocruiser Maiden Flight (Antoinette Donnelly — WOR)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>WOR (Mutual)</strong><br>1949-08-26<br>12:45 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Manhattan Sponsors</strong><br><em>New York Daily News</em></td>\n<td><strong>Antoinette Donnelly</strong>, <strong>Pan Am Flight Crew</strong></td>\n<td><strong>WOR Special Features</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Talk&quot;, &quot;Interview&quot;, &quot;Travelogue&quot;, &quot;Aviation&quot;, &quot;Americana&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Around New York with Antoinette Donnelly, your guide to city life, fashion, and exciting events! Columnist Antoinette Donnelly recounts her exhilarating inaugural flight aboard the luxurious double-decker Pan American Boeing 377 Stratocruiser over Manhattan, detailing the lower-deck cocktail lounge and pressurized passenger comfort.&quot;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>On_Stage_1954.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The Prize Fighter</code>, <code>The Prize Fighter On Stage</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Prize Fighter (Elliott &amp; Cathy Lewis — CBS On Stage)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS/KNX)</strong><br>1954-08-26<br>9:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Radio Theater Anthology</td>\n<td><strong>Elliott Lewis</strong>, <strong>Cathy Lewis</strong>, <strong>Sheldon Leonard</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Morton Fine</strong>, <strong>David Friedkin</strong>, <strong>George Walsh</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Sports&quot;, &quot;Boxing&quot;, &quot;Romance&quot;, &quot;Americana&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Cathy and Elliott Lewis On Stage, bringing you theater at its best, written, directed, and starring Mr. and Mrs. Radio!&quot; Elliott Lewis stars as a proud middleweight prizefighter struggling with impending blindness who hides his injury from his devoted wife (Cathy Lewis) to fight one final championship bout to secure their financial security.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>CBS_News_1940_Late.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>British Air Raid On Berlin</code>, <code>RAF Bombs Berlin Night News</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;RAF Night Bombing of Berlin Confirmed (Bob Trout &amp; William L. Shirer — CBS News)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC)</strong><br>1940-08-26<br>11:00 PM EDST</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Late-Night News Roundup</td>\n<td><strong>Bob Trout</strong> (Anchor), <strong>William L. Shirer</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS News Special Events</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;News&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Wartime&quot;, &quot;Documentary&quot;, &quot;Public Affairs&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;CBS News, Bob Trout reporting from New York!&quot; Late-night shortwave dispatches confirm that British Bomber Command aircraft dropped high explosives and incendiary bombs across Berlin military targets in direct retaliation for the Luftwaffe&#39;s bombardment of London.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Readers_Digest_1945.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Radio Readers Digest 1945-08-26</code>, <code>Miracle of Boys Town</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Miracle of Father Flanagan&#39;s Boys Town (Conrad Nagel — Campbell&#39;s Soup)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC)</strong><br>1945-08-26<br>9:00 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Campbell Soup Co.</strong><br>Campbell&#39;s Vegetable Soup</td>\n<td><strong>Conrad Nagel</strong>, <strong>Father Edward J. Flanagan</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Robert L. Shayon</strong>, <strong>George Bryan</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Biographical&quot;, &quot;Inspirational&quot;, &quot;Moral&quot;, &quot;Anthology&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;The Campbell Soup Company presents Radio Reader&#39;s Digest, with your host Conrad Nagel!&quot; The inspiring true story of Father Edward J. Flanagan, who founded Boys Town near Omaha, Nebraska on the revolutionary principle that &#39;there is no such thing as a bad boy&#39;, transforming juvenile delinquents through trust and community.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Men_At_Sea_1945.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Voyage to Kingspoint</code>, <code>Merchant Marine Kings Point</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Voyage to Kings Point (Frank Lovejoy — U.S. Maritime Commission Men at Sea)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WEAF)</strong><br>1945-08-26<br>6:30 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>U.S. Maritime Comm.</strong><br>War Shipping Administration</td>\n<td><strong>Frank Lovejoy</strong>, <strong>Ted Osborne</strong>, <strong>Luis Van Rooten</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Allan Sloane</strong>, <strong>John M. Wyatt</strong>, <strong>Don Wilson</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Maritime&quot;, &quot;Docudrama&quot;, &quot;Military&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Men at Sea! The heroic story of the United States Merchant Marine and the men who keep the sea lanes open!&quot; In &#39;Voyage to Kings Point&#39;, a young cadet midshipman trains at the U.S. Merchant Marine Academy, sailing his liberty ship through wartime submarine-infested waters to deliver vital supplies to Allied armies across the Pacific.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 26</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 26</strong>: 215</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
