    "markdown": "# Archival Dispatch: August 26 Calendar Walk — Abie's Irish Rose, Tennessee Ernie Ford, and Joe E. Brown\n\n**Date**: 2026-08-26  \n**Author**: radio index  \n**Tags**: August 26, Calendar Walk, Abies Irish Rose, Anne Nichols, Sydney Smith, Julie Bourke, Charlie Cantor, Drene Shampoo, Heartbeat Theatre, Don MacLaughlin, Salvation Army, GI Journal, Joe E Brown, Mel Blanc, Kay Kyser, AFRS, Ford Road Show, Tennessee Ernie Ford, Ford Motor Co, Johnson Family, Jimmy Scribner, Betty and Bob, Alternate Titles, Original Filenames\n\n---\n\n## August 26 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 164)\n\nThis archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, serial multi-part narrative arcs, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on **August 26** across American network, syndicated, and armed forces radio, Anne Nichols' classic *Abie's Irish Rose* for Drene Shampoo, Tennessee Ernie Ford on *The Ford Road Show*, Joe E. Brown and Mel Blanc entertaining troops on AFRS *G.I. Journal*, Don MacLaughlin on Salvation Army's *Heartbeat Theatre*, Jimmy Scribner's 22-voice tour de force on *The Johnson Family*, and *Betty and Bob* (1944–1958):\n\n---\n\n## 1. *August 26 Archival Inventory (Increment 164)*\n\n| Original Circulating Filename & Alternate Titles | Canonical Title | Network, Airdate & Showtime | Sponsor & Commercial Ads | Credited Cast & Performers | Director, Writers & Crew | Genres | Story-First Plot Synopsis |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `Abies_Irish_Rose_1944.mp3` <br>*Alt*: `Abie's Irish Rose 1944-08-26`, `Twins Birthday Celebration` | **\"The Twins' Birthday Celebration (Sydney Smith & Julie Bourke — Drene Shampoo)\"** | **NBC (WEAF)**<br>1944-08-26<br>8:00 PM EWT | **Procter & Gamble**<br>Drene Shampoo (\"Special Drene\") | **Sydney Smith** (Abie), **Julie Bourke** (Rosemary) | **Anne Nichols**, **Rip Van Ronkel**, **Howard Petrie** | `[\"Comedy\", \"Sitcom\", \"Domestic\", \"Family\", \"Americana\"]` | \"Drene Shampoo presents Anne Nichols' beloved American comedy, Abie's Irish Rose!\" Solomon Levy and Patrick Murphy engage in uproarious grandfatherly rivalry while shopping for competing extravagant birthday gifts for the twins, Patrick Joseph and Rebecca, for Drene Shampoo. |\n| `Heartbeat_Theatre_1956.mp3` <br>*Alt*: `Of Men and Angels`, `Of Men and Angels Heartbeat` | **\"Of Men and Angels (Don MacLaughlin — The Salvation Army Heartbeat Theatre)\"** | **Syndicated**<br>1956-08-26<br>(Salvation Army #18) | **The Salvation Army**<br>Spiritual Public Service | **Don MacLaughlin**, **Joy Geffen**, **Lawson Zerbe** | **Henry Hayward**, **Don Morrow** | `[\"Drama\", \"Religious\", \"Inspirational\", \"Moral\", \"Anthology\"]` | \"The Salvation Army presents Heartbeat Theatre! Inspiring stories of human struggle and faith!\" In 'Of Men and Angels', an embittered, cynical surgeon facing malpractice accusations rediscovers spiritual purpose and compassion through a dedicated Salvation Army mission nurse treating inner-city tenement families. |\n| `GI_Journal_1944.mp3` <br>*Alt*: `AFRS Joe E Brown`, `GI Journal Program 57` | **\"Command Performance G.I. Journal #57 (Joe E. Brown & Mel Blanc — AFRS)\"** | **AFRS (Shortwave)**<br>1944-08-26<br>(AFRS Program #57) | **U.S. War Dept.**<br>Allied Forces Service | **Joe E. Brown**, **Mel Blanc** (Sad Sack), **Linda Darnell** | **Capt. Austin Peterson**, **Kay Kyser** | `[\"Variety\", \"Comedy\", \"Wartime\", \"Military\", \"Big Band\"]` | \"G.I. Journal! The overseas soldiers' own newspaper of the air, brought to you by Armed Forces Radio!\" Big-mouthed Hollywood comic Joe E. Brown serves as Editor-in-Chief, trading wartime gags with Mel Blanc as Private Sad Sack, featuring pin-up girl Linda Darnell, swing tunes from Kay Kyser's band, and vocal numbers from The King Sisters. |\n| `Ford_Road_Show_1958.mp3` <br>*Alt*: `First Song - What Is This Thing Called Love?`, `Ford Show` | **\"What Is This Thing Called Love? (Tennessee Ernie Ford — Ford Motor Co.)\"** | **CBS (WCBS)**<br>1958-08-26<br>7:00 PM EDT | **Ford Motor Co.**<br>1958 Fairlane & Thunderbird | **Tennessee Ernie Ford**, **Jack Fascinato Orch.** | **Bud Cole**, **Frank Goss** | `[\"Music\", \"Country\", \"Americana\", \"Vocal\", \"Variety\"]` | \"The Ford Road Show, starring Tennessee Ernie Ford, brought to you by Ford Motor Company!\" Ol' Ern welcomes listeners with 'Bless your pea-pickin' hearts!', performing Cole Porter's 'What Is This Thing Called Love?', country gospel hymns, and folksy humor backed by Jack Fascinato's Orchestra for Ford. |\n| `Johnson_Family_1949.mp3` <br>*Alt*: `Brother Johnson Interviews Counterfeiter`, `Johnson Family` | **\"Brother Johnson Interviews the Counterfeiter (Jimmy Scribner — Mutual Johnson Family)\"** | **Mutual (WOR)**<br>1949-08-26<br>11:15 AM EDT | **Sustaining**<br>Solo Voice Folk Serial | **Jimmy Scribner** (Solo Voice / All 22 Roles) | **Jimmy Scribner**, **Ken Powell** | `[\"Comedy\", \"Sitcom\", \"Domestic\", \"Americana\", \"Short Form\"]` | \"The Johnson Family, with all characters created and played by Jimmy Scribner!\" In Chickawaukee, Brother Johnson and Lawyer Jenkins interrogate a smooth-talking itinerant stranger passing counterfeit twenty-dollar bills at the general store, only to have the suspect attempt to pay his legal retainer with bogus banknotes. |\n| `Betty_Bob_1947.mp3` <br>*Alt*: `Betty and Bob 1947-08-26`, `Bob's Mining Venture Crisis` | **\"Bob's Mining Venture Crisis (Episode #42 — Alice Frost & Spencer Bentley — Betty and Bob)\"** | **Syndicated**<br>1947-08-26<br>(Hummert Drama #42) | **Local Merchants**<br>Daytime Romance Serial | **Alice Frost** (Betty), **Spencer Bentley** (Bob) | **Frank & Anne Hummert**, **Don Lowe** | `[\"Drama\", \"Soap Opera\", \"Domestic\", \"Romance\", \"Short Form\"]` | \"Betty and Bob, the dramatic story of a young married couple facing life together!\" Bob Drake's new mining partnership is threatened when an unscrupulous syndicate attempts to seize his mineral rights, prompting Betty to rally their loyal friends to preserve the family's financial future. Note: Multi-part serial narrative arc *(Bob's Mining Venture Crisis — Episode 42)*. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. *Archival Verification Summary*\n\n- **Target Calendar Day**: August 26\n- **Broadcasts Resolved This Increment**: 6\n- **Cumulative Resolved on August 26**: 209\n- **Target Repositories Synchronized**: `radioindex.org-meta` and `radioindex.org-blog`\n"
