    "html": "<h2>August 26 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 163)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, serial multi-part narrative arcs, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 26</strong> across American network radio, Peg Lynch&#39;s domestic sitcom masterpiece <em>The Couple Next Door</em> across three classic episodes (postal rates, Shakespearean roasts, and lawnmower petunias), Chic Young&#39;s <em>Blondie</em> starring Penny Singleton and Arthur Lake (bathtub goldfish for Camels and accidental handcuffs for Super Suds), and Percy Faith conducting the <em>Carnation Contented Hour</em> (1940–1960):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 26 Archival Inventory (Increment 163)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Couple_Next_Door_1958.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Postal Rate Increase</code>, <code>Postal Rates Couple Next Door</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Postal Rate Increase (Peg Lynch &amp; Alan Bunce — Ex-Lax The Couple Next Door)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1958-08-26<br>10:05 AM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Ex-Lax, Inc.</strong><br>The Chocolated Laxative</td>\n<td><strong>Peg Lynch</strong> (Peg), <strong>Alan Bunce</strong> (Jim)</td>\n<td><strong>Peg Lynch</strong>, <strong>Frank Dodge</strong>, <strong>Dan Donaldson</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Sitcom&quot;, &quot;Domestic&quot;, &quot;Americana&quot;, &quot;Short Form&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;The Couple Next Door, created and written by Peg Lynch, starring Peg Lynch and Alan Bunce!&quot; When the U.S. Post Office announces a one-cent first-class postage rate increase, Peg attempts to save pennies by organizing a chaotic neighborhood hand-delivery postal system that costs Jim triple in lost time.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Couple_Next_Door_1959.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Stratford Upon Avon</code>, <code>Stratford-upon-Avon</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Stratford-upon-Avon &amp; Elizabethan Roasts (Peg Lynch &amp; Alan Bunce — CBS)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1959-08-26<br>10:05 AM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Suburban Domestic Sitcom</td>\n<td><strong>Peg Lynch</strong> (Peg), <strong>Alan Bunce</strong> (Jim)</td>\n<td><strong>Peg Lynch</strong>, <strong>Frank Dodge</strong>, <strong>Dan Donaldson</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Sitcom&quot;, &quot;Domestic&quot;, &quot;Americana&quot;, &quot;Short Form&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;The Couple Next Door, starring Peg Lynch and Alan Bunce!&quot; Inspired by an upcoming community Shakespeare festival, Peg attempts to immerse the Piper household in Elizabethan culture by speaking exclusively in rhyming iambic pentameter and cooking authentic 16th-century roasted mutton for Jim.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Couple_Next_Door_1960.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Mrs. Piper Mows The Lawn</code>, <code>Mrs Piper Mows Lawnmower</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Mrs. Piper Mows the Lawn (Peg Lynch &amp; Alan Bunce — CBS Couple Next Door)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1960-08-26<br>10:05 AM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Suburban Domestic Sitcom</td>\n<td><strong>Peg Lynch</strong> (Peg), <strong>Alan Bunce</strong> (Jim)</td>\n<td><strong>Peg Lynch</strong>, <strong>Frank Dodge</strong>, <strong>Dan Donaldson</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Sitcom&quot;, &quot;Domestic&quot;, &quot;Americana&quot;, &quot;Short Form&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;The Couple Next Door, starring Peg Lynch and Alan Bunce!&quot; Determined to prove suburban self-reliance, Peg takes over the balky gasoline power lawnmower to groom the front yard, inadvertently carving circular crop patterns across the neighbor&#39;s prized prize-winning petunias.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Carnation_1946.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Episode</code>, <code>Carnation Contented Hour 1946-08-26</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Percy Faith &amp; Buddy Clark (Josephine Antoine — Carnation Contented Hour)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Red (WEAF)</strong><br>1946-08-26<br>10:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Carnation Company</strong><br>Carnation Evaporated Milk</td>\n<td><strong>Percy Faith</strong>, <strong>Buddy Clark</strong>, <strong>Josephine Antoine</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Erwin Wasey</strong>, <strong>Vincent Pelletier</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Pop Standards&quot;, &quot;Vocal&quot;, &quot;Classical&quot;, &quot;Big Band&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;The Carnation Contented Hour, from contented cows! Maestro Percy Faith leads the Carnation Orchestra and Contented Chorus in sparkling symphonic pop melodies, featuring crooner Buddy Clark singing &#39;They Say It&#39;s Wonderful&#39; and soprano Josephine Antoine singing classical airs for Carnation Milk.&quot;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Blondie_1940.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Blondie 1940-08-26</code>, <code>Dagwood Bathtub Goldfish</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Dagwood&#39;s Bathtub Goldfish Farm (Penny Singleton &amp; Arthur Lake — Camel Blondie)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC/KNX)</strong><br>1940-08-26<br>7:30 PM EDST</td>\n<td><strong>R.J. Reynolds</strong><br>Camel Cigarettes &amp; Prince Albert</td>\n<td><strong>Penny Singleton</strong> (Blondie), <strong>Arthur Lake</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Chic Young</strong>, <strong>Don Bernard</strong>, <strong>Bill Goodwin</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Sitcom&quot;, &quot;Domestic&quot;, &quot;Family&quot;, &quot;Comics&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Camels present Blondie, starring Penny Singleton as Blondie and Arthur Lake as Dagwood!&quot; Dagwood invents an absurd get-rich-quick plan to breed prize Japanese goldfish in the Bumstead family bathtub, triggering furious confrontations with boss Mr. Dithers when the fish overflow into the living room for Camel Cigarettes.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Blondie_1945.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Blondie Handcuffs Her Husband</code>, <code>Super Suds Blondie</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Blondie Handcuffs Her Husband (Penny Singleton &amp; Arthur Lake — Super Suds)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC/KNX)</strong><br>1945-08-26<br>8:00 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Colgate-Palmolive</strong><br>Super Suds (&quot;Lots More Suds&quot;)</td>\n<td><strong>Penny Singleton</strong>, <strong>Arthur Lake</strong>, <strong>Hanley Stafford</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Chic Young</strong>, <strong>Don Bernard</strong>, <strong>Howard Petrie</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Sitcom&quot;, &quot;Domestic&quot;, &quot;Family&quot;, &quot;Comics&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Super Suds presents Blondie, starring Penny Singleton and Arthur Lake!&quot; While demonstrating antique police handcuffs from the attic, Blondie accidentally locks Dagwood&#39;s wrists together just before an emergency dinner with wealthy prospective architectural client Mr. Dithers for Super Suds.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 26</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 26</strong>: 203</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
