    "html": "<h2>August 26 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 151)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, serial multi-part narrative arcs, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 26</strong> across American network, Claudette Colbert and Don DeFore in <em>Without Reservations</em> alongside Helen Twelvetrees on <em>Lux Radio Theatre</em> for Lux Soap, William Conrad confronting frontier exploitation in Les Crutchfield&#39;s <em>Gunsmoke</em> for L&amp;M, Sydney Smith solving a locked-office slaying in <em>The Adventures of Ellery Queen</em> for Anacin, and WWII Radio News commentaries (1935–1956):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 26 Archival Inventory (Increment 151)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Lux_Theatre_1935.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The Church Mouse</code>, <code>Helen Twelvetrees Lux Theatre</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Church Mouse (Helen Twelvetrees &amp; Henry Daniell — Lux Theatre)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Blue (WJZ)</strong><br>1935-08-26<br>9:30 PM EDST</td>\n<td><strong>Lever Brothers</strong><br>Lux Toilet Soap &amp; Flakes</td>\n<td><strong>Helen Twelvetrees</strong>, <strong>Henry Daniell</strong>, <strong>Donald Meek</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Ladislaus Fodor</strong>, <strong>Antony Stanford</strong>, <strong>Louis Silvers</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Romance&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Classics&quot;, &quot;Broadway&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;The Lux Radio Theatre, originating live from the stage of the NBC Studio in New York!&quot; Helen Twelvetrees stars in Ladislaus Fodor&#39;s charming romantic comedy <em>The Church Mouse</em>, playing an impoverished but determined Viennese typist who talks her way into the office of a powerful Austrian banker, transforming his business and winning his heart for Lux Toilet Soap.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Lux_Theatre_1946.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Without Reservations</code>, <code>Claudette Colbert Without Reservations</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Without Reservations (Claudette Colbert &amp; Don DeFore — Lux Radio Theatre)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (KNX/WCBS)</strong><br>1946-08-26<br>9:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Lever Brothers</strong><br>Lux Toilet Soap (&quot;9 out of 10&quot;)</td>\n<td><strong>Claudette Colbert</strong>, <strong>Don DeFore</strong>, <strong>Robert Rockwell</strong></td>\n<td><strong>William Keighley</strong>, <strong>Sanford Barnett</strong>, <strong>Louis Silvers</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Romance&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Hollywood&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Americana&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;From Hollywood, the Lux Radio Theatre presents Claudette Colbert and Don DeFore in Without Reservations!&quot; Host William Keighley welcomes Claudette Colbert as a famous intellectual novelist traveling anonymously by cross-country train to Hollywood, who falls for an irreverent Marine flyer played by Don DeFore without revealing that her best-selling book mocks men just like him for Lux Soap.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Radio_News_1943.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>MBS Paul Schubert</code>, <code>Paul Schubert Kharkov 1943</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Battle of Kharkov &amp; Mediterranean Strategy (Paul Schubert — Mutual)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1943-08-26<br>10:15 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Military News Analysis</td>\n<td><strong>Paul Schubert</strong> (Naval Analyst/Commentator)</td>\n<td><strong>Mutual News Special Events</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;News&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Wartime&quot;, &quot;Military&quot;, &quot;Public Affairs&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Mutual presents Paul Schubert with the latest military and naval analysis!&quot; Naval commentator Paul Schubert assesses the strategic significance of the Soviet Red Army&#39;s liberation of Kharkov and breaks down Allied joint operations in the Mediterranean preparing for the invasion of the Italian mainland.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Radio_News_1945.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>CBS World News Today</code>, <code>MacArthur Tokyo Occupation</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Allied Fleet in Sagami Bay &amp; Tokyo Occupation (Douglas Edwards — CBS)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC)</strong><br>1945-08-26<br>2:00 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Transpacific News Roundup</td>\n<td><strong>Douglas Edwards</strong> (Anchor), <strong>Webley Edwards</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS News Special Events</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;News&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Wartime&quot;, &quot;Documentary&quot;, &quot;Public Affairs&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;CBS World News Today, Douglas Edwards reporting from New York!&quot; Shortwave correspondents report on the massing of the Allied Third Fleet in Sagami Bay outside Tokyo and final logistics for General Douglas MacArthur&#39;s airborne arrival at Atsugi Airfield ahead of Japan&#39;s formal surrender.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Gunsmoke_1956.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>No Sale</code>, <code>William Conrad Gunsmoke 1956</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;No Sale (William Conrad as Matt Dillon — L&amp;M Gunsmoke)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1956-08-26<br>6:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Liggett &amp; Myers</strong><br>L&amp;M Filter Cigarettes</td>\n<td><strong>William Conrad</strong> (Matt Dillon), <strong>Parley Baer</strong>, <strong>Georgia Ellis</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Les Crutchfield</strong>, <strong>Norman Macdonnell</strong>, <strong>George Walsh</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Americana&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Around Dodge City and into the territory on West, there&#39;s just one way to handle the killers and the spoilers, and that&#39;s with a U.S. Marshal and the smell of Gunsmoke! When an impoverished prairie homesteader&#39;s desperate wife attempts to sell their young daughter to a disreputable saloon keeper, Marshal Matt Dillon intervenes before frontier violence erupts in Dodge City for L&amp;M Cigarettes.&quot;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Ellery_Queen_1944.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The Mayor and the Corpse</code>, <code>Anacin Ellery Queen 1944</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Mayor and the Corpse (Sydney Smith as Ellery Queen — Anacin)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WEAF)</strong><br>1944-08-26<br>7:30 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Whitehall Pharmacal</strong><br>Anacin Fast Pain Relief</td>\n<td><strong>Sydney Smith</strong> (Ellery Queen), <strong>Santos Ortega</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Frederic Dannay</strong>, <strong>Manfred B. Lee</strong>, <strong>George Zachary</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Whodunit&quot;, &quot;Puzzle&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;The Adventures of Ellery Queen, brought to you by Anacin! Ellery Queen challenges the radio audience and a guest armchair detective panel to match wits and solve the murder of a corrupt municipal mayor discovered stabbed to death inside his locked office safe during a stormy re-election eve for Anacin.&quot;</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 26</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 26</strong>: 131</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
