    "html": "<h2>August 25 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 79)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, serial multi-part narrative arcs, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 25</strong> across American network, three thrilling eras of Superman superhero serials, big band hit parade broadcasts starring Vaughn Monroe, and authentic South African police procedural flying squad action (1943–1972):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 25 Archival Inventory (Increment 79)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Superman_1943_08_25.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Civil Air Patrol Part 6</code>, <code>Superman Submarine Hunt</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Civil Air Patrol: Coastal Submarine Hunt (Part 6 — Bud Collyer — Kellogg&#39;s Pep)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1943-08-25<br>5:15 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>The Kellogg Co.</strong><br>Kellogg&#39;s Pep — Vitamins</td>\n<td><strong>Bud Collyer</strong> (Superman), <strong>Jackie Kelk</strong> (Jimmy Olsen)</td>\n<td><strong>George Lowther</strong> (Dir.), <strong>Jackson Beck</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Superhero&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Juvenile&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Aviation&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In Part 6 of <em>The Civil Air Patrol</em>, Clark Kent and Jimmy Olsen discover enemy submarine signaling stations positioned along the Atlantic coastline, guiding Superman to intercept Axis U-boats for Kellogg&#39;s Pep.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Superman_1944_08_25.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Ghosts of Air Part 9</code>, <code>Phantom Bombers Superman</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Ghosts of the Air: The Invisible Fleet (Part 9 — Bud Collyer — Kellogg&#39;s Pep)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1944-08-25<br>5:15 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>The Kellogg Co.</strong><br>Kellogg&#39;s Pep Cereal</td>\n<td><strong>Bud Collyer</strong> (Superman), <strong>Joan Alexander</strong> (Lois)</td>\n<td><strong>George Lowther</strong>, <strong>Jackson Beck</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Superhero&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Juvenile&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Science Fiction&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In Part 9 of <em>Ghosts of the Air</em>, Superman confronts an airborne fleet of radar-invisible phantom bombers sabotaging Allied transport lines, destroying the master control tower to save Metropolis for Kellogg&#39;s Pep.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Superman_1948_08_25.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Mystery Letter Part 8</code>, <code>Harbor Bomb Threat</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Mystery of the Letter: The Harbor Bomb Threat (Part 8 of 11 — Bud Collyer — Mutual)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1948-08-25<br>5:15 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Juvenile Superhero Serial</td>\n<td><strong>Bud Collyer</strong> (Superman), <strong>Jack Grimes</strong> (Jimmy Olsen)</td>\n<td><strong>George Lowther</strong>, <strong>Jackson Beck</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Superhero&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Juvenile&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In Part 8 of <em>The Mystery of the Letter</em>, Clark Kent tracks an extortionist ring that mailed an encrypted ransom note threatening to blow up Metropolis harbor, using his X-ray vision to pinpoint the hidden explosive trigger.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Camel_Caravan_1951.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>First Song Because of You</code>, <code>Vaughn Monroe Camel 1951</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Because of You (Vaughn Monroe &amp; The Moon Maids — Camel Cigarettes)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1951-08-25<br>7:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>R.J. Reynolds</strong><br>Camel — &quot;More Doctors Smoke&quot;</td>\n<td><strong>Vaughn Monroe Orchestra</strong>, <strong>The Moon Maids</strong></td>\n<td><strong>William Esty Co.</strong>, <strong>Joe Bigelow</strong>, <strong>Gene Hamilton</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Big Band&quot;, &quot;Pop&quot;, &quot;Vocal&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;It&#39;s the Camel Caravan starring Vaughn Monroe!&quot; Deep-voiced baritone sensation Vaughn Monroe leads his orchestra and The Moon Maids in romantic chart-toppers including &#39;Because of You&#39;, &#39;Sound Off&#39;, and &#39;Racing with the Moon&#39; for Camel Cigarettes.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Squad_Cars_1968.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Never Too Old To Die</code>, <code>Squad Cars South Africa 1968</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Never Too Old to Die (General Motors Squad Cars — Springbok)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Springbok Radio</strong><br>1968-08-25<br>7:30 PM SAST</td>\n<td><strong>General Motors</strong><br>Chevrolet &amp; Holden</td>\n<td><strong>Patrick Mynhardt</strong>, <strong>Colin Fish</strong>, <strong>Dale Cutts</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Hugh Rouse</strong> (Writer), <strong>David Gooden</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Procedural&quot;, &quot;Police&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;They walk by night... they walk by day... the men of the South African Police Squad Cars!&quot; Radio patrol flying squads in Johannesburg investigate the armed burglary of an elderly wealthy recluse, cornering an ex-convict safe cracker before he can flee the Witwatersrand.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Squad_Cars_1972.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Models Jealous Husband</code>, <code>Squad Cars Durban 1972</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Model&#39;s Jealous Husband (General Motors Squad Cars — Springbok)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Springbok Radio</strong><br>1972-08-25<br>8:00 PM SAST</td>\n<td><strong>General Motors</strong><br>Chevrolet Ranger &amp; Opel</td>\n<td><strong>Colin Fish</strong>, <strong>Hal Orlandini</strong>, <strong>Shelagh Holliday</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Hugh Rouse</strong>, <strong>David Gooden</strong>, <strong>David Davies</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Procedural&quot;, &quot;Police&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Patrol units race to an upscale Durban suburban estate following reports of gunfire, intervening in a violent confrontation involving an enraged, armed husband stalking his fashion model wife.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 25</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 25</strong>: 89</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
