    "html": "<h2>August 25 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 110)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, serial multi-part narrative arcs, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 25</strong> across American network, three classic newspaper hardboiled cases of <em>Casey, Crime Photographer</em> across two lead actors (Staats Cotsworth &amp; Darren McGavin) and two sponsors (Anchor Hocking &amp; Philip Morris), Peter Tinniswood&#39;s uproarious Antarctic cricket memoirs on BBC Radio 4, Joseph Cotten &amp; Teresa Wright on <em>Armed Forces Radio Theater</em>, and children&#39;s fables on <em>The Story Lady</em> (1945–1981):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 25 Archival Inventory (Increment 110)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Tales_Long_Room_1981.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Polar Games</code>, <code>The Brigadier Polar Games</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Polar Games by Peter Tinniswood (Robin Bailey as The Brigadier — BBC)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>BBC Radio 4</strong><br>1981-08-25<br>6:30 PM BST</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Cricket Comedy Monologues</td>\n<td><strong>Robin Bailey</strong> (The Brigadier)</td>\n<td><strong>Peter Tinniswood</strong> (Writer), <strong>John Tydeman</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;British&quot;, &quot;Satire&quot;, &quot;Sports&quot;, &quot;Cricket&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Tales from a Long Room, by Peter Tinniswood, starring Robin Bailey as the Brigadier!&quot; The pompous, cricket-obsessed Brigadier recounts his uproarious memoirs of the legendary 1912 expedition when English gentlemen attempted to play a five-day test cricket match on the Antarctic ice cap with emperor penguins serving as fielders.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Story_Lady_1947.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The Story Lady: The Shaggiest Dog in the World</code>, <code>The Shaggiest Dog in the World</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Shaggiest Dog in the World (Georgene O&#39;Donnell — The Story Lady)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WEAF)</strong><br>1947-08-25<br>9:15 AM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Children&#39;s Storytelling</td>\n<td><strong>Georgene O&#39;Donnell</strong> (Story Lady), <strong>Rosa Rio</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Children&#39;s Programs</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Children&quot;, &quot;Storytelling&quot;, &quot;Fable&quot;, &quot;Family&quot;, &quot;Educational&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Here comes The Story Lady!&quot; The Story Lady reads the delightful children&#39;s fable &#39;The Shaggiest Dog in the World&#39;, recounting how a kindly, overgrown sheepdog with mop-like fur wins the hearts of the villagers by rescuing lost kittens during a summer rainstorm.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Casey_1949_Live.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Casey The Snow Ball</code>, <code>The Snowball Live 1949</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Snowball (Staats Cotsworth as Flashgun Casey — Anchor Hocking Glass)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1949-08-25<br>9:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Anchor Hocking</strong><br>Fire-King Ovenware</td>\n<td><strong>Staats Cotsworth</strong> (Casey), <strong>Jan Miner</strong> (Ann)</td>\n<td><strong>Alonzo Deen Cole</strong>, <strong>John Dietz</strong>, <strong>Bob Hite</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Newspaper&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Anchor Hocking Glass presents Casey, Crime Photographer!&quot; <em>Morning Express</em> photographer Flashgun Casey and reporter Ann Williams visit the Blue Note Cafe before untangling a runaway &#39;snowball&#39; extortion racket where small-time blackmail against a Broadway producer snowballs into a sensational nightclub shooting.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Casey_1949_West.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The Snow Ball</code>, <code>The Snowball West Coast Repeat</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Snowball (West Coast Repeat — Casey, Crime Photographer)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (KNX)</strong><br>1949-08-25<br>8:30 PM PST</td>\n<td><strong>Anchor Hocking</strong><br>Fire-King Heat-Resistant Glass</td>\n<td><strong>Staats Cotsworth</strong> (Casey), <strong>Jan Miner</strong> (Ann)</td>\n<td><strong>Alonzo Deen Cole</strong>, <strong>John Dietz</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Newspaper&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;It&#39;s Fire-King Ovenware time with Casey, Crime Photographer!&quot; In this Pacific network repeat performance, Casey takes crime-scene flashbulb photos that reveal how a seemingly accidental fire at a Broadway theater was deliberately set to cover up an extortion homicide for Fire-King Ovenware.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Casey_1954.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The Moth</code>, <code>Darren McGavin Casey The Moth</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Moth (Darren McGavin as Casey — Philip Morris Cigarettes)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1954-08-25<br>9:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Philip Morris &amp; Co.</strong><br>Philip Morris Cigarettes</td>\n<td><strong>Darren McGavin</strong> (Casey), <strong>Jan Miner</strong> (Ann)</td>\n<td><strong>John Dietz</strong> (Dir.), <strong>Ken Roberts</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Newspaper&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Philip Morris presents Casey, Crime Photographer!&quot; Ace news photographer Casey investigates the suspicious drowning of an eccentric millionaire lepidopterist nicknamed &#39;The Moth&#39;, following a trail of forged wills and stolen rare specimens through the waterfront docks for Philip Morris.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>AFRS_Theater_1945.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Return To Tomorrow</code>, <code>Joseph Cotten Teresa Wright AFRS</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Return to Tomorrow (Joseph Cotten &amp; Teresa Wright — Armed Forces Radio)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>AFRS Hollywood</strong><br>1945-08-25<br>(Overseas Troops)</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>AFRS Morale Broadcast</td>\n<td><strong>Joseph Cotten</strong>, <strong>Teresa Wright</strong>, <strong>Ray Collins</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Wilbur Hatch Orchestra</strong>, <strong>Ken Carpenter</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Romance&quot;, &quot;Military&quot;, &quot;Postwar&quot;, &quot;Hollywood&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;From Hollywood, the Armed Forces Radio Service presents Armed Forces Radio Theater!&quot; Hollywood stars Joseph Cotten and Teresa Wright star in &#39;Return to Tomorrow&#39;, a touching romantic drama about a discharged wounded infantry veteran who returns home to rebuild his life, find forgiveness, and reclaim his future with his devoted high-school sweetheart.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 25</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 25</strong>: 275</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
