    "html": "<h2>August 25 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 102)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, serial multi-part narrative arcs, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 25</strong> across American network, Ernest Tubb &amp; Minnie Pearl live from Nashville&#39;s Ryman Auditorium for Prince Albert, Karl Swenson as Central Police disguise master Mr. Chameleon for Bayer Aspirin, Westinghouse&#39;s scientific investigation into the 18th-century &#39;Mechanical Turk&#39; chess automaton, and Hollywood stars on Father Peyton&#39;s <em>Family Theater</em> (1947–1956):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 25 Archival Inventory (Increment 102)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Grand_Ole_Opry_1956.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>You All Come And See Us</code>, <code>Ernest Tubb Minnie Pearl 1956</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Live from the Ryman Auditorium: Ernest Tubb &amp; Minnie Pearl (Prince Albert)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WSM)</strong><br>1956-08-25<br>9:30 PM CDT</td>\n<td><strong>R.J. Reynolds</strong><br>Prince Albert Tobacco</td>\n<td><strong>Ernest Tubb</strong>, <strong>Minnie Pearl</strong>, <strong>Ray Price</strong></td>\n<td><strong>WSM Operations</strong>, <strong>Grant Turner</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Country&quot;, &quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Live from the Ryman Auditorium in Nashville, Tennessee, it&#39;s the Grand Ole Opry, brought to you by Prince Albert Smoking Tobacco!&quot; Ernest Tubb and his Texas Troubadours perform honky-tonk anthems, Ray Price sings &#39;Crazy Arms&#39;, and Cousin Minnie Pearl cracks up the crowd with Grinders Switch gossip for Prince Albert.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Mr_Chameleon_1948.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The Case Of His Brothers Murderer</code>, <code>Mr Chameleon Bayer 1948</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Case of His Brother&#39;s Murderer (Karl Swenson as Mr. Chameleon — Bayer)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1948-08-25<br>8:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sterling Drug Inc.</strong><br>Genuine Bayer Aspirin</td>\n<td><strong>Karl Swenson</strong> (Mr. Chameleon), <strong>Frank Butler</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Frank &amp; Anne Hummert</strong>, <strong>Howard Claney</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Procedural&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Mr. Chameleon... the famous and dreaded disguise-artist of Central Police Headquarters, brought to you by Genuine Bayer Aspirin!&quot; Disguised as a waterfront dockworker, Mr. Chameleon tracks an elusive underworld assassin who framed an innocent man for the revenge murder of his own brother.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Aunt_Mary_1947.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Dr Whitney Changes His Mind</code>, <code>Aunt Mary Albers Flapjack</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Dr. Whitney Changes His Mind About Kitty (Jane Morgan as Aunt Mary — Albers)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Pacific</strong><br>1947-08-25<br>2:30 PM PST</td>\n<td><strong>Albers Milling / Carnation</strong><br>Albers Flapjack Flour</td>\n<td><strong>Jane Morgan</strong> (Aunt Mary), <strong>Fred Howard</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Virginia Crosby</strong>, <strong>Jimmy Wallington</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Soap Opera&quot;, &quot;Domestic&quot;, &quot;Family&quot;, &quot;Human Interest&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Aunt Mary, the story of a woman whose life is dedicated to the service of others, presented by Albers Flapjack Flour!&quot; In the small town of Oakdale, Aunt Mary mediates a tense medical crisis as Dr. Whitney admits he misjudged young nurse Kitty&#39;s capabilities during an emergency hospital surgery.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Chuck_Wagon_1950.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Oh For The Life Of A Cowboy</code>, <code>Chuck Wagon Jamboree 1950</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Oh, For the Life of a Cowboy (The Chuck Wagon Gang — Mutual)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1950-08-25<br>12:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Western Music</td>\n<td><strong>The Chuck Wagon Gang</strong>, <strong>Bob Wills Playboys</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual Midwest</strong>, <strong>Jack Brickhouse</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Country&quot;, &quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Vocal&quot;, &quot;Harmony&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Gather round the campfire for the Chuck Wagon Jamboree!&quot; Frontier string bands and cowboy vocalists perform jaunty trail songs and western swing instrumentals, opening with &#39;Oh, For the Life of a Cowboy&#39; alongside traditional frontier spirituals.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Adventures_Research_1953.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The Automatic Chess Player</code>, <code>Mechanical Turk Westinghouse</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Automatic Chess Player: The Mechanical Turk (Paul Shannon — Westinghouse)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Westinghouse</strong><br>1953-08-25<br>(KDKA Pittsburgh)</td>\n<td><strong>Westinghouse Corp.</strong><br>Science Education</td>\n<td><strong>Paul Shannon</strong> (Narrator), <strong>Dr. Phillips Thomas</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Westinghouse Research Laboratories</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Science&quot;, &quot;Documentary&quot;, &quot;Educational&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Technology&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Adventures in Research, presented by Westinghouse!&quot; Dr. Phillips Thomas explores the fascinating 18th-century historical mystery of Wolfgang von Kempelen&#39;s &#39;Mechanical Turk&#39;, an alleged chess-playing automaton that defeated Benjamin Franklin and Napoleon, revealing the ingenious clockwork illusion.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Family_Theater_1954.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Beauty and the Brain</code>, <code>Stephen McNally Family Theater</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Beauty and the Brain (Host Stephen McNally — Father Peyton&#39;s Family Theater)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1954-08-25<br>9:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Family Theater</td>\n<td><strong>Stephen McNally</strong> (Host), <strong>Jeff Chandler</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Father Patrick Peyton</strong>, <strong>David Young</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Inspirational&quot;, &quot;Romantic Comedy&quot;, &quot;Human Interest&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Family Theater, dedicated to the rediscovery of the soul of America!&quot; Hollywood leading man Stephen McNally hosts &#39;Beauty and the Brain&#39;, a charming romantic comedy about a brilliant research physicist who falls head-over-heels for a glamorous Broadway showgirl, proving that love defies scientific logic.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 25</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 25</strong>: 227</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
