    "html": "<h2>August 25 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 101)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, serial multi-part narrative arcs, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 25</strong> across American network, Bing Crosby &amp; Rosemary Clooney&#39;s breezy morning vocal duets, two eras of domestic comedy on <em>Father Knows Best</em> starring Robert Young (Maxwell House &amp; Post Bran Flakes), Sir Ralph Richardson in Arnold Bennett&#39;s <em>The Judgement</em>, outback aviation on <em>The Flying Doctor</em>, and Broadway belter Ethel Merman on <em>The Royal Gelatin Hour</em> (1938–1961):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 25 Archival Inventory (Increment 101)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Bing_Rosemary_1961.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>I Feel A Song Coming On</code>, <code>Bing and Rosie 1961</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;I Feel a Song Coming On (Bing Crosby &amp; Rosemary Clooney — CBS)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1961-08-25<br>10:45 AM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Morning Pop Variety</td>\n<td><strong>Bing Crosby</strong>, <strong>Rosemary Clooney</strong>, <strong>Buddy Cole</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Bill Morrow</strong>, <strong>Murdo MacKenzie</strong>, <strong>George Walsh</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Pop&quot;, &quot;Vocal&quot;, &quot;Easy Listening&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;The Bing Crosby-Rosemary Clooney Show!&quot; Pop music titans Bing Crosby and Rosemary Clooney trade effortless vocal duets and witty banter, performing &#39;I Feel a Song Coming On&#39;, &#39;Fancy Meeting You Here&#39;, and &#39;Love Is Here to Stay&#39; with the Buddy Cole Trio for CBS.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Flying_Doctor_1959.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Episode</code>, <code>Outback Flood Rescue</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Outback Flood Rescue (James McKechnie as Dr. Halliday — BBC)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>BBC Light</strong><br>1959-08-25<br>7:30 PM BST</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Outback Aviation Drama</td>\n<td><strong>James McKechnie</strong> (Dr. Halliday), <strong>Bill Kerr</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Ernest Dudley</strong>, <strong>Charles Chilton</strong>, <strong>Sidney Torch</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Medical&quot;, &quot;Aviation&quot;, &quot;Australian&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;The Flying Doctor, based on the real-life work of the Royal Flying Doctor Service of Australia!&quot; Dr. Greg Halliday pilots his medical biplane through blinding monsoon rains to parachute emergency surgical supplies to an isolated sheep station cut off by outback floodwaters.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Royal_Gelatin_1938_2.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Royal Gelatin Hour Rudy Vallee</code>, <code>Ethel Merman Royal Gelatin</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Guest Broadway Star Ethel Merman (Rudy Vallee — Royal Gelatin)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Red (WEAF)</strong><br>1938-08-25<br>8:00 PM EDST</td>\n<td><strong>Standard Brands Inc.</strong><br>Royal Gelatin &amp; Puddings</td>\n<td><strong>Rudy Vallee</strong>, <strong>Ethel Merman</strong>, <strong>Eric Blore</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Joe Bigelow</strong> (Dir.), <strong>Jimmy Wallington</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Variety&quot;, &quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Broadway&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Vocal&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;The Royal Gelatin Hour, starring Rudy Vallee!&quot; Broadway&#39;s brassy superstar Ethel Merman belts showstopping Broadway anthems, while dry British comic Eric Blore trades hilarious high-society barbs with Rudy for Royal Gelatin Desserts.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Theatre_Royal_1954.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Theatreroyal54 08 2547thejudgement</code>, <code>Ralph Richardson The Judgement</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Judgement by Arnold Bennett (Starring Sir Ralph Richardson — Mutual)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (Towers)</strong><br>1954-08-25<br>9:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>British Classic Drama</td>\n<td><strong>Sir Ralph Richardson</strong>, <strong>Laurence Payne</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Arnold Bennett</strong>, <strong>Harry Alan Towers</strong>, <strong>Sidney Torch</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;British&quot;, &quot;Classics&quot;, &quot;Victorian&quot;, &quot;Anthology&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;From London, Theatre Royal, starring Sir Ralph Richardson!&quot; Sir Ralph Richardson stars in Arnold Bennett&#39;s poignant Edwardian drama <em>The Judgement</em>, portraying an inflexible magistrate whose harsh public moral pronouncements are challenged when his own son is brought before the bench.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Father_Knows_Best_1949.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Father Knows Best 1949-08-25</code>, <code>Jim Takes Over Cooking</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Jim Takes Over the Family Cooking (Robert Young — Maxwell House)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1949-08-25<br>8:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>General Foods</strong><br>Maxwell House Coffee</td>\n<td><strong>Robert Young</strong> (Jim), <strong>June Whitley</strong> (Margaret)</td>\n<td><strong>Ed James</strong>, <strong>Kenneth MacGregor</strong>, <strong>Bill Goodwin</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Sitcom&quot;, &quot;Domestic&quot;, &quot;Family&quot;, &quot;Americana&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Father Knows Best, starring Robert Young, brought to you by Maxwell House Coffee!&quot; When Margaret is bedridden with a summer cold, Jim proudly insists that running a household and cooking three square meals a day is simple, turning the Anderson kitchen into a smoke-filled disaster area for Maxwell House.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Father_Knows_Best_1952.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Skates On The Stairs</code>, <code>Father Knows Best Post Bran</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Roller Skates on the Stairs (Robert Young — Post 40% Bran Flakes)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1952-08-25<br>8:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>General Foods</strong><br>Post&#39;s 40% Bran Flakes</td>\n<td><strong>Robert Young</strong> (Jim), <strong>Jean Vander Pyl</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Ed James</strong>, <strong>Kenneth MacGregor</strong>, <strong>Bill Goodwin</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Sitcom&quot;, &quot;Domestic&quot;, &quot;Family&quot;, &quot;Americana&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Post 40% Bran Flakes presents Father Knows Best!&quot; Jim Anderson launches a household safety campaign after nearly breaking his neck tripping over Bud&#39;s roller skates on the front stairs, only for his elaborate safety rules to trap the family inside their own house for Post Cereals.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 25</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 25</strong>: 221</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
