    "html": "<h2>August 25 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 100 Milestone)</h2>\n<p>This landmark 100th archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, serial multi-part narrative arcs, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 25</strong> across American network, four classic Arkansas rural comedy chronicles with Lum and Abner (Alka-Seltzer &amp; Frigidaire), Frank Morgan&#39;s hilarious academic absent-mindedness on <em>The Fabulous Dr. Tweedy</em>, and western vocal royalty Bob Nolan &amp; The Sons of the Pioneers (1941–1948):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 25 Archival Inventory (Increment 100)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Dr_Tweedy_1946.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Fabulous Dr. Tweedy 1946-08-25</code>, <code>Frank Morgan Dr Tweedy</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Missing Chemistry Grant Check (Frank Morgan — Raleigh Cigarettes)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WEAF)</strong><br>1946-08-25<br>8:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Brown &amp; Williamson</strong><br>Raleigh 903 Cigarettes</td>\n<td><strong>Frank Morgan</strong> (Dr. Tweedy), <strong>Gale Gordon</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Robert Riley Crutcher</strong>, <strong>Helen Mack</strong>, <strong>Bud Heeston</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Sitcom&quot;, &quot;Academic&quot;, &quot;College&quot;, &quot;Domestic&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;The Fabulous Dr. Tweedy, starring that lovable master of confusion, Frank Morgan, brought to you by Raleigh 903 Cigarettes!&quot; Absent-minded college dean Dr. Tweedy creates uproar across Potts College when he misplaces a $50,000 chemistry laboratory endowment check inside a borrowed library textbook for Raleigh Cigarettes.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Lum_Abner_1941_Live.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Operating the Pine Ridge Bank</code>, <code>Lum and Abner Bank 1941</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Operating the Pine Ridge Bank (Part 1 — Chester Lauck &amp; Norris Goff)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Blue (WJZ)</strong><br>1941-08-25<br>8:15 PM EDST</td>\n<td><strong>Miles Laboratories</strong><br>Alka-Seltzer &amp; One-A-Day</td>\n<td><strong>Chester Lauck</strong> (Lum), <strong>Norris Goff</strong> (Abner)</td>\n<td><strong>Chester Lauck</strong>, <strong>Norris Goff</strong>, <strong>Lou Crosby</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Sitcom&quot;, &quot;Rural&quot;, &quot;Americana&quot;, &quot;Dialect&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Listen to Lum and Abner, brought to you by Alka-Seltzer!&quot; In the sleepy Arkansas hamlet of Pine Ridge, Lum and Abner take over management of the local bank at the Jot &#39;Em Down Store, immediately encountering accounting confusion when Squire Skimp attempts to deposit questionable promissory notes.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Lum_Abner_1941_West.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Operate Bank</code>, <code>Pine Ridge Safe Lock-In</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Operating the Pine Ridge Bank (West Coast Repeat — Lum &amp; Abner)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Blue (KGO)</strong><br>1941-08-25<br>8:15 PM PST</td>\n<td><strong>Miles Laboratories</strong><br>Alka-Seltzer &amp; One-A-Day</td>\n<td><strong>Chester Lauck</strong> (Lum), <strong>Norris Goff</strong> (Abner)</td>\n<td><strong>Chester Lauck</strong>, <strong>Norris Goff</strong>, <strong>Lou Crosby</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Sitcom&quot;, &quot;Rural&quot;, &quot;Americana&quot;, &quot;Dialect&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Alka-Seltzer presents Lum and Abner!&quot; In this live Pacific network repeat performance, Lum and Abner attempt to install a foolproof security vault at the Pine Ridge Bank, only for Abner to lock Grandpap inside the store safe during lunch hour.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Lum_Abner_1943.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Cedric Thinks He Has the Measles</code>, <code>Cedric Measles Quarantine</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Cedric Thinks He Has the Measles (Lum &amp; Abner — Alka-Seltzer)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Blue (WJZ)</strong><br>1943-08-25<br>8:15 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Miles Laboratories</strong><br>Alka-Seltzer &amp; One-A-Day</td>\n<td><strong>Chester Lauck</strong> (Cedric), <strong>Norris Goff</strong> (Abner)</td>\n<td><strong>Larry Berns</strong> (Dir.), <strong>Lou Crosby</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Sitcom&quot;, &quot;Rural&quot;, &quot;Americana&quot;, &quot;Dialect&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Lum and Abner, brought to you by Alka-Seltzer!&quot; Clueless Jot &#39;Em Down Store clerk Cedric Weehunt breaks out in red spots and convinces himself he has contracted the measles, causing Lum and Abner to impose a panic-stricken quarantine on the entire store for Alka-Seltzer.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Lum_Abner_1948.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Want To Build Modern Poor House</code>, <code>Pine Ridge Poor House Frigidaire</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Luxurious Pine Ridge Poorhouse (Lum &amp; Abner — Frigidaire)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1948-08-25<br>10:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>General Motors</strong><br>Frigidaire Refrigerators</td>\n<td><strong>Chester Lauck</strong> (Lum), <strong>Norris Goff</strong> (Abner)</td>\n<td><strong>William Burch</strong> (Dir.), <strong>Wendell Niles</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Sitcom&quot;, &quot;Rural&quot;, &quot;Americana&quot;, &quot;Dialect&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Frigidaire presents Lum and Abner!&quot; Lum and Abner propose an extravagant civic project to construct a luxury hotel-style poorhouse in Pine Ridge with swimming pools and valets, driving town treasurer Ben Withers to distraction for Frigidaire.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Sons_Pioneers_1948.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Song of the Bandit</code>, <code>Lucky U Ranch Sons of Pioneers</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Song of the Bandit (Bob Nolan &amp; Sons of the Pioneers — Lucky U Ranch)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Teleways Synd.</strong><br>1948-08-25<br>(KNX Hollywood)</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Western Music</td>\n<td><strong>Bob Nolan</strong>, <strong>Lloyd Perryman</strong>, <strong>Hugh Farr</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Teleways Radio</strong>, <strong>Ken Carson</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Country&quot;, &quot;Vocal&quot;, &quot;Harmony&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;From the Lucky U Ranch in Hollywood, here are the Sons of the Pioneers!&quot; Western vocal giants Bob Nolan and The Sons of the Pioneers perform breathtaking four-part cowboy harmonies and fiery twin-fiddle breakdowns including &#39;Song of the Bandit&#39;, &#39;Chant of the Wanderer&#39;, and &#39;Blue Prairie&#39;.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 25</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 25</strong>: 215</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
