    "html": "<h2>August 24 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 63)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, serial multi-part narrative arcs, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 24</strong> across American network, hardboiled detective mysteries, female-led domestic sitcoms, and live Town Hall political debates (1944–1954):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 24 Archival Inventory (Increment 63)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>My_Friend_Irma_1954.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Janes Suitor</code>, <code>Marie Wilson Irma 1954</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Jane&#39;s High-Society Suitor (Marie Wilson &amp; Cathy Lewis — CBS)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1954-08-24<br>9:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>CBS Sitcom Series</td>\n<td><strong>Marie Wilson</strong> (Irma), <strong>Cathy Lewis</strong> (Jane), <strong>John Brown</strong> (Al)</td>\n<td><strong>Cy Howard</strong> (Creator), <strong>Parke Levy</strong>, <strong>Frank Bingman</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Sitcom&quot;, &quot;Domestic&quot;, &quot;Female Lead&quot;, &quot;Americana&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Well-meaning but hopelessly scatterbrained Irma Peterson attempts to assist roommate Jane Stacy in preparing for a dinner date with a wealthy Wall Street broker, accidentally mixing up the guest list with Al&#39;s racetrack betting bookies.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Falcon_1952_08_24_A.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Case Silent Butler</code>, <code>Falcon Les Damon 1952</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Case of the Silent Butler (Les Damon as The Falcon — NBC)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1952-08-24<br>4:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>NBC Mystery Series</td>\n<td><strong>Les Damon</strong> (The Falcon), <strong>Ken Lynch</strong> (Billy O&#39;Hara)</td>\n<td><strong>Michael Arlen</strong>, <strong>Richard Lewis</strong>, <strong>Ed Herlihy</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Noir&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;The Falcon... that fabulous character, Michael Waring...&quot; Freelance adventurer Michael Waring investigates the mysterious poisoning of an elderly industrialist in a Long Island mansion, where the key witness is a deaf-mute butler who held the secret combination to a looted wall safe.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Falcon_1952_08_24_B.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Silent Butler AFRS</code>, <code>The Falcon 1952</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Case of the Silent Butler (AFRS Rebroadcast — Les Damon)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>AFRS</strong><br>1952-08-24<br>(Rebroadcast)</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Armed Forces Radio</td>\n<td><strong>Les Damon</strong> (The Falcon), <strong>Ken Lynch</strong>, <strong>Mandel Kramer</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Michael Arlen</strong>, <strong>Richard Lewis</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Noir&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Michael Waring outmaneuvers a ruthless ring of blackmailers who framed a wealthy estate&#39;s mute butler for homicide and jewel theft, cracking the case with help from Sergeant Billy O&#39;Hara.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Falcon_1953_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Senators Death Riddle</code>, <code>The Falcon 1953</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Riddle of the Senator&#39;s Murder (George Petrie as The Falcon — Mutual)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1953-08-24<br>8:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Mutual Crime Series</td>\n<td><strong>George Petrie</strong> (Michael Waring), <strong>Robert Dryden</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Michael Arlen</strong>, <strong>Carlo D&#39;Angelo</strong>, <strong>Bob Maurer</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Political&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Returning to Washington D.C. from an undercover overseas intelligence assignment, Michael Waring solves the suspicious midnight rooftop death of an anti-corruption U.S. Senator before state secrets are auctioned to a foreign cartel.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Peter_Salem_1952.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Terrified Trumpet</code>, <code>Peter Salem 1952</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Affair of the Terrified Trumpet (Santos Ortega as Peter Salem — Mutual)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1952-08-24<br>5:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Mutual Mystery Series</td>\n<td><strong>Santos Ortega</strong> (Peter Salem), <strong>Jack Grimes</strong> (Marty)</td>\n<td><strong>Louis Vittes</strong> (Writer), <strong>Himan Brown</strong>, <strong>Frank Waldecker</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Procedural&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;, &quot;Music&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Astute small-town sleuth Peter Salem and young assistant Marty travel to a Manhattan jazz club to investigate deadly threats against a famous trumpet virtuoso whose improvised solos conceal secret underworld numbers racket drop codes.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Town_Meeting_1944.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Post-War Foreign Policy</code>, <code>Town Meeting 1944</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Post-War Foreign Policy &amp; International Peace (George V. Denny Jr. — Reader&#39;s Digest)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Blue (WJZ)</strong><br>1944-08-24<br>8:30 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Reader&#39;s Digest</strong><br>Association Sponsor</td>\n<td><strong>George V. Denny Jr.</strong>, <strong>Sen. Claude Pepper</strong>, <strong>Norman Thomas</strong></td>\n<td><strong>The Town Hall Inc. New York</strong>, <strong>Gene Hamilton</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Public Affairs&quot;, &quot;Debate&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;World War II&quot;, &quot;Politics&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Town Hall Tonight!&quot; Moderator George V. Denny Jr. hosts a fiery live debate from Town Hall New York on America&#39;s post-war foreign policy, international peace organizations, and global economic reconstruction following the impending Allied victory in World War II for Reader&#39;s Digest.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 24</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 24</strong>: 378</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
