    "html": "<h2>August 24 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 57)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, serial multi-part narrative arcs, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 24</strong> across American network, frontline war reporting, screwball detective comedy, and hospital medical drama radio history (1940–1952):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 24 Archival Inventory (Increment 57)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Dr_Kildare_1950_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Young Surgeon Dilemma</code>, <code>Lew Ayres Dr Kildare</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Young Surgeon&#39;s Dilemma (Lew Ayres &amp; Lionel Barrymore — MGM)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>MGM Synd.</strong><br>1950-08-24<br>(WMGM NY)</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>MGM Radio Attractions</td>\n<td><strong>Lew Ayres</strong> (Dr. Kildare), <strong>Lionel Barrymore</strong> (Dr. Gillespie)</td>\n<td><strong>Max Brand</strong> (Creator), <strong>William P. Rousseau</strong>, <strong>Dick Joy</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Medical&quot;, &quot;Hospital&quot;, &quot;Human Interest&quot;, &quot;Anthology&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>At Blair General Hospital, Dr. James Kildare confronts a difficult diagnostic puzzle involving an injured concert pianist whose paralysis may be psychological rather than physical, seeking the gruff wisdom of mentor Dr. Leonard Gillespie.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Clyde_Beatty_1950_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>King Of Clowns</code>, <code>Clyde Beatty Kelloggs 1950</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The King of Clowns (Clyde Beatty Big Cat Circus — Kellogg&#39;s)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1950-08-24<br>5:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Kellogg&#39;s Cereals</strong><br>Kellogg&#39;s Corn Flakes</td>\n<td><strong>Clyde Beatty</strong>, <strong>Hal Peary</strong>, <strong>Lurene Tuttle</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Shirley Thomas</strong> (Producer), <strong>Paul Pierce</strong>, <strong>Frank Goss</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Circus&quot;, &quot;Animals&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Family&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>World-renowned big cat trainer Clyde Beatty investigates mysterious sabotage under the big top after the circus&#39;s beloved lead clown is targeted during a daring three-ring lion act.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Clyde_Beatty_1952_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Escape Black Leopard</code>, <code>Clyde Beatty 1952</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Escape of the Black Leopard (Starring Clyde Beatty — Mutual)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1952-08-24<br>5:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Circus Adventure Drama</td>\n<td><strong>Clyde Beatty</strong> (Self), <strong>Herb Vigran</strong>, <strong>Parley Baer</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Shirley Thomas</strong> (Producer), <strong>Paul Pierce</strong>, <strong>Frank Goss</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Circus&quot;, &quot;Animals&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Family&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Clyde Beatty uses his whip, chair, and extraordinary instincts when a dangerous black leopard escapes its traveling circus cage near a crowded county fair midway.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Thin_Man_1945_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>TCOT Talking Horse</code>, <code>Nick Nora Maxwell House</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Case of the Talking Horse (Les Tremayne &amp; Claudia Morgan — Maxwell House)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC)</strong><br>1945-08-24<br>8:30 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>General Foods Corp.</strong><br>Maxwell House Coffee</td>\n<td><strong>Les Tremayne</strong> (Nick), <strong>Claudia Morgan</strong> (Nora), <strong>Asta</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Dashiell Hammett</strong>, <strong>Himan Brown</strong>, <strong>Tom Shirley</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>While vacationing in Saratoga, sophisticated sleuth Nick Charles and Nora investigate the murder of a wealthy racehorse trainer whose prized stallion is rumored to talk and reveal racetrack betting fixers for Maxwell House Coffee.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Murrow_1940_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Air Raid Over Thames</code>, <code>Murrow Battle of Britain</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;This Is London: Air Raid Over the Thames (Edward R. Murrow — CBS)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC)</strong><br>1940-08-24<br>6:45 PM EDST</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>CBS Transatlantic News</td>\n<td><strong>Edward R. Murrow</strong> (London), <strong>Elmer Davis</strong> (New York)</td>\n<td><strong>CBS News Special Events Team in London &amp; New York</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;News&quot;, &quot;Journalism&quot;, &quot;World War II&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Live Broadcast&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;This... is London.&quot; Edward R. Murrow delivers a gripping live rooftop broadcast during a massive Luftwaffe bombing raid on London, describing anti-aircraft shrapnel lighting up the night sky, sirens wailing over the Thames, and the calm resilience of British civilians during the height of the Battle of Britain.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Archie_Andrews_1946_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Archies Summer Jalopy</code>, <code>Archie Andrews Swift 1946</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Archie&#39;s Summer Jalopy Disaster (Bob Hastings as Archie — Swift&#39;s)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WEAF)</strong><br>1946-08-24<br>10:30 AM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Swift &amp; Company</strong><br>Peter Pan Peanut Butter</td>\n<td><strong>Bob Hastings</strong> (Archie), <strong>Hal Stone</strong> (Jughead), <strong>Gloria Mann</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Bob Montana</strong> (Creator), <strong>Kenneth MacGregor</strong>, <strong>Kenneth Banghart</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Sitcom&quot;, &quot;Teen&quot;, &quot;High School&quot;, &quot;Americana&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Riverdale teen Archie Andrews and loyal pal Jughead Jones attempt to rebuild an old jalopy to impress Veronica Lodge, resulting in an explosive carburetor backfire that coats Mr. Lodge&#39;s flower garden in motor grease.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 24</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 24</strong>: 342</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
