    "html": "<h2>August 24 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 37)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 24</strong> across American network, daytime variety, and hardboiled detective radio history (1948–1962):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 24 Archival Inventory (Increment 37)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Lum_Abner_1948_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Abner Lizabeth Move In</code>, <code>Lum Abner Frigidaire 1948</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Abner and Elizabeth Move In with Lum (Chester Lauck &amp; Norris Goff — Frigidaire)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1948-08-24<br>10:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>General Motors</strong><br>Frigidaire Appliances</td>\n<td><strong>Chester Lauck</strong> (Lum), <strong>Norris Goff</strong> (Abner)</td>\n<td><strong>Chester Lauck &amp; Norris Goff</strong>, <strong>Larry Berns</strong>, <strong>Wendell Niles</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Sitcom&quot;, &quot;Rural&quot;, &quot;Americana&quot;, &quot;Dialect&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Down in Pine Ridge, Arkansas, chaos erupts at the Jot &#39;Em Down Store when Abner and Elizabeth temporarily move into Lum&#39;s bachelor quarters following a fumigation mishap at their farmhouse.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Texas_Rangers_1952_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Three Victims</code>, <code>Joel McCrea Texas Rangers 1952</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Three Victims (Starring Joel McCrea as Ranger Jace Pearson — Wheaties)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1952-08-24<br>6:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>General Mills, Inc.</strong><br>Wheaties — &quot;Champions&quot;</td>\n<td><strong>Joel McCrea</strong> (Ranger Pearson), <strong>Herb Vigran</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Stacy Keach Sr.</strong> (Producer/Dir.), <strong>Joel Murcott</strong>, <strong>Hal Gibney</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Police&quot;, &quot;Procedural&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Detective&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Texas Ranger Jace Pearson uses ballistic trajectory analysis and tire tread casts to track down a cold-blooded highway bandit whose armed service station holdups leave three innocent victims in their wake.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Bing_Rosie_1961_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Breezin Along With Breeze</code>, <code>Bing Crosby Rosemary Clooney 1961</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Breezin&#39; Along with the Breeze (Bing Crosby &amp; Rosemary Clooney — CBS)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1961-08-24<br>10:45 AM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Daytime Music Showcase</td>\n<td><strong>Bing Crosby</strong>, <strong>Rosemary Clooney</strong>, <strong>Buddy Cole Trio</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Bill Morrow</strong> (Producer/Director), <strong>Jim Ameche</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Vocal&quot;, &quot;Easy Listening&quot;, &quot;Jazz&quot;, &quot;Duet&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Bing Crosby and Rosemary Clooney share easygoing humor and sublime vocal harmonies accompanied by Buddy Cole&#39;s swinging organ trio, performing &#39;Breezin&#39; Along with the Breeze&#39; and &#39;Lazy River&#39;.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Bing_Rosie_1962_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Carolina In The Morning</code>, <code>Bing Rosie Duet 1962</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Carolina in the Morning (Bing Crosby &amp; Rosemary Clooney — CBS)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1962-08-24<br>10:45 AM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Daytime Music Showcase</td>\n<td><strong>Bing Crosby</strong>, <strong>Rosemary Clooney</strong>, <strong>Buddy Cole Trio</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Bill Morrow</strong> (Producer/Director), <strong>Buddy Cole</strong> (Arranger)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Vocal&quot;, &quot;Easy Listening&quot;, &quot;Jazz&quot;, &quot;Duet&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>America&#39;s favorite musical pairing Bing Crosby and Rosemary Clooney delight daytime listeners with playful banter and sunny jazz duets of &#39;Carolina in the Morning&#39; and &#39;Pennies from Heaven&#39; with Buddy Cole&#39;s Trio.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>The_Lineup_1950_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Arson case body found</code>, <code>Lineup Arson Murder 1950</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Warehouse Arson and Murder Case (Lt. Ben Guthrie — The Lineup)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1950-08-24<br>10:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Police Procedural</td>\n<td><strong>Bill Johnstone</strong> (Lt. Guthrie), <strong>Wally Maher</strong> (Sgt. Grebb)</td>\n<td><strong>Blake Edwards</strong> (Writer), <strong>Jaime del Valle</strong>, <strong>Dan Cubberly</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Police&quot;, &quot;Procedural&quot;, &quot;Noir&quot;, &quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Ladies and gentlemen, the story you are about to hear is true...&quot; Lieutenant Ben Guthrie and Sergeant Matt Grebb of the San Francisco Police Department investigate a scorched warehouse blaze, discovering a charred corpse that turns an apparent insurance fire into a first-degree homicide investigation.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Martin_Kane_1952_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Bar Bombing Martin Kane</code>, <code>Lee Tracy Sano Cigarettes</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Manhattan Bar Bombing (Starring Lee Tracy as Martin Kane — Sano Cigarettes)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1952-08-24<br>4:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>U.S. Tobacco Co.</strong><br>Sano &amp; Model Pipe Tobacco</td>\n<td><strong>Lee Tracy</strong> (Martin Kane), <strong>Walter Kinsella</strong>, <strong>Horace McMahon</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Ted Hediger</strong> (Writer), <strong>Frank Burns</strong>, <strong>Fred Cole</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Noir&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Hardboiled Manhattan private eye Martin Kane drops into Happy McMann&#39;s tobacco shop for pipe tobacco before investigating a deadly Manhattan tavern explosion after witnesses report a mysterious blonde delivered a ticking package.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 24</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 24</strong>: 222</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
