    "html": "<h2>August 24 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 27)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 24</strong> across American network, Australian commercial syndication, and British BBC Radio 4 comedy history (1939–1976):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 24 Archival Inventory (Increment 27)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>FBI_1955_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Double Play AFRTS</code>, <code>Martin Blaine FBI 1955</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Double Play (Starring Martin Blaine as Agent Jim Taylor — FBI)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS / AFRTS</strong><br>1955-08-24<br>8:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>CBS Crime Drama / AFRTS</td>\n<td><strong>Martin Blaine</strong> (Agent Taylor), <strong>Ralph Bell</strong>, <strong>Mandel Kramer</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Frederick L. Collins</strong>, <strong>Louis Vittes</strong>, <strong>Betty Mandeville</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Police&quot;, &quot;Procedural&quot;, &quot;True Crime&quot;, &quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Federal&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>FBI special agents track an elusive interstate gambling ring that uses high-stakes baseball score rigging and coded Western Union telegraphs to fleece bookmakers across three state lines.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>FBI_1958_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The Muscle Man</code>, <code>FBI Strong Arm Racket</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Muscle Man (Starring Martin Blaine as Agent Jim Taylor — FBI)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1958-08-24<br>6:05 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>CBS Crime Drama</td>\n<td><strong>Martin Blaine</strong> (Agent Taylor), <strong>Leon Janney</strong>, <strong>Robert Dryden</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Louis Vittes</strong> (Writer), <strong>Betty Mandeville</strong>, <strong>Warren Sweeney</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Police&quot;, &quot;Procedural&quot;, &quot;True Crime&quot;, &quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Federal&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Federal agents stage an undercover sting to dismantle an extortion syndicate after a ruthless dockside muscle man begins terrorizing independent trucking companies along the Eastern Seaboard.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Star_Time_1946_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Operation Monsoon</code>, <code>Herbert Marshall Frigidaire</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Operation Monsoon (Host Herbert Marshall with John Beal — Frigidaire)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC)</strong><br>1946-08-24<br>8:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>General Motors</strong><br>Frigidaire Home Appliances</td>\n<td><strong>Herbert Marshall</strong> (Host), <strong>John Beal</strong>, <strong>Martha Scott</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Robert L. Redd</strong> (Director), <strong>Carmen Dragon</strong>, <strong>Wendell Niles</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Aviation&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Romance&quot;, &quot;Anthology&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Host Herbert Marshall presents John Beal and Martha Scott in an aviation adventure, following a valiant transport pilot who battles typhoon winds, failing hydraulics, and a tropical fever epidemic to fly penicillin to an isolated Pacific coral atoll.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Fu_Manchu_1939_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Fu Manchu Appears</code>, <code>Harold Huber Fu Manchu 1939</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Fu Manchu Appears (Chapter 33 — Starring Harold Huber as Fu Manchu)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Radio Attractions</strong><br>1939-08-24<br>(Show #33)</td>\n<td><strong>Regional Advertisers</strong><br>Beverage Sponsors</td>\n<td><strong>Harold Huber</strong> (Fu Manchu), <strong>Hanley Stafford</strong>, <strong>Gale Gordon</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Sax Rohmer</strong> (Author), <strong>Himan Brown</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Thriller&quot;, &quot;Exotic&quot;, &quot;Pulp&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Master criminal mastermind Dr. Fu Manchu materializes in London to threaten the British Empire with a deadly venomous fungus, forcing Sir Denis Nayland Smith and Dr. Petrie into a desperate trap beneath the Limehouse docks.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Deadline_AU_1954_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Musical Chairs The Age</code>, <code>Grace Gibson Deadline 1954</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Musical Chairs: The Age Corruption Probe (Ray Barrett — Grace Gibson Deadline)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Grace Gibson Synd.</strong><br>1954-08-24<br>(2UW Sydney)</td>\n<td><strong>Australian Advertisers</strong><br>Commercial Sponsors</td>\n<td><strong>Ray Barrett</strong>, <strong>Moray Powell</strong>, <strong>John Cazabon</strong></td>\n<td><strong>John Saul</strong> (Director), <strong>Charles Tingwell</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Journalism&quot;, &quot;True Crime&quot;, &quot;Australian&quot;, &quot;Docudrama&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Based on front-page reportage from Melbourne&#39;s <em>The Age</em>, a crusading Australian investigative journalist uncovers political bribery and corruption in municipal land rezoning tenders.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Dads_Army_1976_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Two and a Half Feathers</code>, <code>Arthur Lowe Dads Army 1976</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Two and a Half Feathers (Arthur Lowe &amp; John Le Mesurier — Dad&#39;s Army)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>BBC Radio 4</strong><br>1976-08-24<br>12:27 PM BST</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>BBC Radio 4 Comedy</td>\n<td><strong>Arthur Lowe</strong> (Capt. Mainwaring), <strong>John Le Mesurier</strong>, <strong>Clive Dunn</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Jimmy Perry &amp; David Croft</strong>, <strong>Michael Knowles &amp; Harold Snoad</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Sitcom&quot;, &quot;British&quot;, &quot;Military&quot;, &quot;Satire&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>When a mysterious former comrade accuses Corporal Jones of cowardice during the 1898 Battle of Omdurman in the Sudan, Captain Mainwaring convenes an eccentric Home Guard court of inquiry in Walmington-on-Sea to clear Jones&#39;s decorated military honor.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 24</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 24</strong>: 162</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
