    "html": "<h2>August 24 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 22)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 24</strong> across American network, USAAF military, and CBS international shortwave history (1937–1949):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 24 Archival Inventory (Increment 22)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Heart_Gold_1937_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Heart Of Gold</code>, <code>Arch Oboler Heart of Gold</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Heart of Gold (Arch Oboler Drama — NBC Blue)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Blue (WJZ)</strong><br>1937-08-24<br>8:00 PM EDST</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Dramatic Presentation</td>\n<td><strong>Florence Malone</strong>, <strong>James Meighan</strong>, <strong>Karl Swenson</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Arch Oboler</strong> (Writer), <strong>Anton M. Leader</strong>, <strong>Alois Havrilla</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Anthology&quot;, &quot;Psychological&quot;, &quot;Romance&quot;, &quot;Moral Tale&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In Arch Oboler&#39;s probing moral drama, an embittered Wall Street tycoon facing financial ruin is saved from despair by an impoverished flower girl whose boundless generosity forces him to confront his lifelong greed.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>London_Dark_1940_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>London After Dark</code>, <code>Murrow London After Dark</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;London After Dark (Edward R. Murrow &amp; CBS Correspondents Live in the Blitz)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC)</strong><br>1940-08-24<br>6:30 PM EDST</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>CBS News Live Relay</td>\n<td><strong>Edward R. Murrow</strong>, <strong>Larry Lesueur</strong>, <strong>Eric Sevareid</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS News Special Events Unit Transatlantic Transmission</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;News&quot;, &quot;Documentary&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;World War II&quot;, &quot;Journalism&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>A historic live transatlantic broadcast across wartime London as Edward R. Murrow and CBS correspondents take mobile microphones to Piccadilly Circus, Trafalgar Square, and air raid shelters to capture the sights and sounds of British resilience during the Blitz.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>USAAF_1944_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>USAF Presents - Photo Recon</code>, <code>Reagan Photo Reconnaissance</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Photo Reconnaissance Mission (Narrated by Ronald Reagan — USAAF Special)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>USAAF / AFRS</strong><br>1944-08-24<br>(Special Report)</td>\n<td><strong>U.S. War Dept</strong><br>Army Air Forces Presentation</td>\n<td><strong>Ronald Reagan</strong> (Narrator), <strong>William Holden</strong></td>\n<td><strong>USAAF First Motion Picture Unit</strong>, <strong>Ken Carpenter</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Docudrama&quot;, &quot;Military&quot;, &quot;Aviation&quot;, &quot;World War II&quot;, &quot;Educational&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Narrated by Captain Ronald Reagan, this dramatic USAAF documentary chronicles the perilous unarmed low-altitude aerial reconnaissance mission of an F-5 Lightning over fortified German positions in Normandy to photograph enemy troop movements.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Ray_Bolger_1945_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Ray Bolger Sinatra 1945</code>, <code>Ray Bolger Rexall</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Ray Bolger Show: Guest Frank Sinatra (Rexall)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC)</strong><br>1945-08-24<br>10:00 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Rexall Drug Company</strong><br>&quot;Good Health from Rexall&quot;</td>\n<td><strong>Ray Bolger</strong>, <strong>Frank Sinatra</strong> (Guest), <strong>Elvia Allman</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Arthur Stander &amp; Jack Douglas</strong>, <strong>Dave Swift</strong>, <strong>Howard Petrie</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;, &quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Vocal&quot;, &quot;Tap Dance&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Comic dancing maestro Ray Bolger welcomes Frank Sinatra for a raucous half-hour of Broadway show tunes, slapstick dance coaching, and their classic wartime vocal duet of &#39;Saturday Night Is the Loneliest Night of the Week&#39;.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Deadline_1947_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Deadline Mystery - Apartment</code>, <code>Apartment Racket Mutual</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Apartment Racket (Deadline Mystery — Mutual)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1947-08-24<br>7:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Mystery Presentation</td>\n<td><strong>Joseph Julian</strong>, <strong>Santos Ortega</strong>, <strong>Mandel Kramer</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Jerry McGill</strong> (Writer), <strong>Charles Powers</strong>, <strong>Carl Caruso</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Investigative&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>An undercover investigative newspaper reporter poses as a desperate veteran seeking housing in post-war Manhattan, exposing a corrupt subletting racket that extorts exorbitant bonuses from unsuspecting apartment seekers.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Tell_Neighbor_1949_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Tell Your Neighbor</code>, <code>Fred Beck ABC 1949</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Tell Your Neighbor: Everyday Kindness (Fred Beck — ABC)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>ABC (WJZ)</strong><br>1949-08-24<br>10:00 AM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Human Interest Presentation</td>\n<td><strong>Fred Beck</strong> (Host / Storyteller), <strong>Bob Fleming</strong></td>\n<td><strong>ABC Hollywood Production</strong>, <strong>Don Lowe</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Human Interest&quot;, &quot;Talk&quot;, &quot;Americana&quot;, &quot;Storytelling&quot;, &quot;Community&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Folklorist and columnist Fred Beck shares heartwarming real-life anecdotes of everyday kindness, community goodwill, and humorous neighborhood eccentricities submitted by listeners across America.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 24</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 24</strong>: 132</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
