    "html": "<h2>August 24 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 18)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 24</strong> across American network, AFRS military, and South African Springbok Radio broadcasting history (1943–1973):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 24 Archival Inventory (Increment 18)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Superman_1943_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Civil Air Patrol 5</code>, <code>Bud Collyer Superman 1943</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Civil Air Patrol (Part 5 — Starring Bud Collyer as Superman — Kellogg&#39;s PEP)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1943-08-24<br>5:15 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Kellogg Company</strong><br>Kellogg&#39;s PEP Cereal</td>\n<td><strong>Bud Collyer</strong> (Superman), <strong>Joan Alexander</strong> (Lois)</td>\n<td><strong>Jerry Siegel &amp; Joe Shuster</strong>, <strong>George Lowther</strong>, <strong>Jackson Beck</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Superhero&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Science Fiction&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Juvenile&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In part five of the wartime <em>Civil Air Patrol</em> arc, Clark Kent and the junior air spotters track down a clandestine Axis shortwave transmitter broadcasting Allied ship departures from a coastal lighthouse, triggering Superman&#39;s aerial rescue when enemy agents trap the cadets in the flooded tower.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Superman_1944_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Ghosts of the Air 8</code>, <code>Invisible Bomber Superman</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Ghosts of the Air (Part 8 — Starring Bud Collyer as Superman — Kellogg&#39;s PEP)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1944-08-24<br>5:15 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Kellogg Company</strong><br>Kellogg&#39;s PEP Cereal</td>\n<td><strong>Bud Collyer</strong> (Superman), <strong>Jackie Kelk</strong> (Jimmy Olsen)</td>\n<td><strong>Siegel &amp; Shuster</strong>, <strong>B.P. Freeman</strong>, <strong>Jackson Beck</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Superhero&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Science Fiction&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Juvenile&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In chapter eight of <em>Ghosts of the Air</em>, the Man of Steel intercepts an experimental invisible bomber terrorizing coastal shipping corridors, battling blinding electronic radar jamming high above Metropolis to guide a disabled transport plane safely to ground.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Superman_1945_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The Black Market 1</code>, <code>Superman Black Market 1945</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Black Market (Part 1 — Starring Bud Collyer as Superman — Kellogg&#39;s PEP)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1945-08-24<br>5:15 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Kellogg Company</strong><br>Kellogg&#39;s PEP Cereal</td>\n<td><strong>Bud Collyer</strong> (Superman), <strong>Julian Noa</strong> (Perry White)</td>\n<td><strong>Siegel &amp; Shuster</strong>, <strong>B.P. Freeman</strong>, <strong>Jackson Beck</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Superhero&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Science Fiction&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Juvenile&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In chapter one of a new postwar arc, Daily Planet reporter Clark Kent uncovers a dangerous black market racket diverting critical baby formula and penicillin shipments from city hospitals, vowing to hunt down the syndicate&#39;s shadowy kingpin.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Superman_1948_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Mystery of the Letter 7</code>, <code>Superman Letter Part 7</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Mystery of the Letter (Part 7 of 11 — Starring Bud Collyer as Superman)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1948-08-24<br>5:15 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Mutual Adventure Series</td>\n<td><strong>Bud Collyer</strong> (Superman), <strong>Jackie Kelk</strong>, <strong>Joan Alexander</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Siegel &amp; Shuster</strong>, <strong>Jessica Maxwell</strong>, <strong>Jackson Beck</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Superhero&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Science Fiction&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Juvenile&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In chapter seven of <em>The Mystery of the Letter</em>, Jimmy Olsen is captured by counterfeiters operating in an abandoned waterfront brewery, forcing Clark Kent to use his x-ray vision to pinpoint the boy&#39;s location before a dynamite fuse reaches a hidden ammunition cache.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Command_Perf_1948_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Marion Hutton Jack Carson</code>, <code>Command Performance 342</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Command Performance #342: Jack Carson, Marion Hutton &amp; Arthur Treacher (AFRS)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>AFRS Unit</strong><br>1948-08-24<br>(Show #342)</td>\n<td><strong>U.S. War Dept</strong><br>Armed Forces Radio Service</td>\n<td><strong>Jack Carson</strong> (Host), <strong>Marion Hutton</strong>, <strong>Arthur Treacher</strong></td>\n<td><strong>AFRS Hollywood Unit</strong>, <strong>Ken Carpenter</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Variety&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Big Band&quot;, &quot;Vocal&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Hollywood funnyman Jack Carson hosts an all-star variety hour for American servicemen overseas, trading frantic insults with Arthur Treacher and introducing swing singer Marion Hutton and the Pied Pipers.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Squad_Cars_1973_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The Suicide Man</code>, <code>Springbok Squad Cars 1973</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Suicide Man (Colin Fish Drama — Springbok Radio Squad Cars)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Springbok Radio</strong><br>1973-08-24<br>8:00 PM SAST</td>\n<td><strong>General Motors</strong><br>Chevrolet &amp; Delco Batteries</td>\n<td><strong>Adrian Steed</strong>, <strong>Douglas Bristow</strong>, <strong>Patrick Mynhardt</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Colin Fish</strong> (Writer/Director), <strong>Hugh Rouse</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Police&quot;, &quot;Procedural&quot;, &quot;True Crime&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Flying Squad patrol officers in Johannesburg race against time to talk down a despondent diamond courier threatening to jump from a 15th-floor skyscraper ledge, uncovering a deadly corporate embezzlement blackmail plot behind his despair.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 24</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 24</strong>: 108</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
