    "html": "<h2>August 24 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 13)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 24</strong> across American network and British BBC Home Service broadcasting history (1939–1959):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 24 Archival Inventory (Increment 13)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Best_Sellers_1945_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Rickshaw Boy Part 5</code>, <code>Keye Luke Bret Morrison</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Rickshaw Boy (Part 5 — Series Finale Starring Keye Luke &amp; Bret Morrison)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>ABC (WJZ)</strong><br>1945-08-24<br>3:00 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>ABC Literary Adaptation</td>\n<td><strong>Keye Luke</strong> (Xiangzi), <strong>Bret Morrison</strong> (Narrator)</td>\n<td><strong>Lao She</strong> (Author), <strong>Robert Newman</strong>, <strong>Marx Loeb</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Literature&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Asian&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In the dramatic concluding chapter of Lao She&#39;s acclaimed novel, optimistic Beijing rickshaw puller Xiangzi battles relentless poverty, corrupt warlord soldiers, and harsh winters in his determined struggle to purchase his own rickshaw.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Widder_Brown_1950_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Humphries Discuss Jim</code>, <code>Florence Freeman Bayer</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Humphries Family Conflict (Starring Florence Freeman as Ellen Brown — Bayer)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1950-08-24<br>4:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sterling Drug Inc.</strong><br>Bayer Aspirin</td>\n<td><strong>Florence Freeman</strong> (Ellen Brown), <strong>Wendy Drew</strong>, <strong>Ned Wever</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Frank &amp; Anne Hummert</strong>, <strong>Frank Gallop</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Soap Opera&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Romance&quot;, &quot;Domestic&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In Simpsonville, widowed mother Ellen Brown faces agonizing heartbreak as the wealthy Humphries family attempts to intervene in her complicated courtship with Jim, threatening the happiness of her tea room business and children.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Two_Clue_1945_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Noisy Corpse 9</code>, <code>Jeff Penny Spencer Post</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Case of the Noisy Corpse (Chapter 9 — Post&#39;s 40% Bran Flakes)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC)</strong><br>1945-08-24<br>2:00 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>General Foods</strong><br>Post&#39;s 40% Bran Flakes</td>\n<td><strong>Ned Wever</strong> (Jeff Spencer), <strong>Louise Fitch</strong> (Penny)</td>\n<td><strong>Harry Ingram</strong> (Writer), <strong>Donald Peterson</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In chapter nine of <em>The Case of the Noisy Corpse</em>, husband-and-wife sleuths Jeff and Penny Spencer search a creaky funeral home basement at midnight, dodging a shadowy prowler who is desperately trying to retrieve an incriminating coded letter.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Desert_Island_1959_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Charles Mackerras</code>, <code>Roy Plomley Mackerras</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Desert Island Discs: Charles Mackerras (Roy Plomley — BBC Home Service)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>BBC Home Serv.</strong><br>1959-08-24<br>1:10 PM BST</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>BBC Cultural Feature</td>\n<td><strong>Roy Plomley</strong> (Host), <strong>Charles Mackerras</strong> (Conductor)</td>\n<td><strong>Roy Plomley</strong> (Creator), <strong>Monica Chapman</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Interview&quot;, &quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Classical&quot;, &quot;Talk&quot;, &quot;British&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Australian-born conductor Charles Mackerras joins host Roy Plomley on the mythical desert island, sharing his eight favorite classical discs (including Janáček and Mozart), a luxury telescope, and the complete orchestral scores of Handel.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Your_Radio_1959_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Portrait of Jennie</code>, <code>Herbert Marshall Barbara Rush</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Portrait of Jennie (Host Herbert Marshall with Barbara Rush — Your Radio Theater)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1959-08-24<br>8:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>NBC Dramatic Series</td>\n<td><strong>Herbert Marshall</strong> (Host), <strong>Barbara Rush</strong>, <strong>Jeffrey Lynn</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Robert Nathan</strong> (Author), <strong>Kenneth MacGregor</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Romance&quot;, &quot;Fantasy&quot;, &quot;Anthology&quot;, &quot;Theater&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Host Herbert Marshall presents a radio dramatization of Robert Nathan&#39;s lyrical fantasy <em>Portrait of Jennie</em>, following a struggling Manhattan painter who finds artistic inspiration and supernatural love with a mysterious girl in Central Park.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Yukon_1939_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Gold Cache Ambush</code>, <code>Sergeant Preston 1939</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Gold Cache Ambush (Starring Jay Michael as Sgt. Preston &amp; King)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>WXYZ / Mutual</strong><br>1939-08-24<br>7:30 PM EDST</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Local Detroit Advertisers</td>\n<td><strong>Jay Michael</strong> (Sgt. Preston), <strong>King the Wonder Dog</strong></td>\n<td><strong>George W. Trendle &amp; Fran Striker</strong>, <strong>Bob Hite</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Canadian&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Police&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Mountie Sergeant William Preston and his wonder dog King brave a blinding Klondike blizzard to track two murderous claim jumpers who dynamited an elderly prospector&#39;s hidden gold cache on Moose Creek.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 24</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 24</strong>: 78</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
