    "html": "<h2>August 24 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 05)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 24</strong> across American network and Treasury syndication broadcasting history (1941–1958):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 24 Archival Inventory (Increment 05)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Greatest_Story_1947_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Call Not Man Fool</code>, <code>Fulton Oursler Greatest Story</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Call Not Any Man a Fool: Parable of the Rich Fool (Goodyear)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>ABC (WJZ)</strong><br>1947-08-24<br>6:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Goodyear Tire</strong><br>Goodyear Commercial-Free</td>\n<td><strong>Warren Parker</strong> (Jesus), <strong>Karl Swenson</strong>, <strong>John Sylvester</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Fulton Oursler</strong> (Creator), <strong>Marx Loeb</strong>, <strong>Leonard Joy</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Religious&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Anthology&quot;, &quot;Biblical&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>A reverent dramatization of Christ&#39;s teachings from the Sermon on the Mount, focusing on the Parable of the Rich Fool and the spiritual folly of hoarding worldly treasures while neglecting the soul.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Henry_Morgan_1949_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Summer Vacation Report</code>, <code>Henry Morgan Vitalis</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Summer Vacation Report (Henry Morgan with Arnold Stang &amp; Art Carney — Vitalis)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1949-08-24<br>9:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Bristol-Myers</strong><br>Vitalis &amp; Sal Hepatica</td>\n<td><strong>Henry Morgan</strong>, <strong>Arnold Stang</strong>, <strong>Alice Pearce</strong>, <strong>Art Carney</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Henry Morgan &amp; Aaron Ruben</strong>, <strong>Milton DeLugg</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Satire&quot;, &quot;Sketch&quot;, &quot;Parody&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Acerbic satirist Henry Morgan skewers sponsor commercials and summer boardwalk tourist traps, featuring neurotic complaints from Gerard (Arnold Stang) and zany parodies of Broadway travelogues.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Guest_Star_1952_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>You Go To My Head</code>, <code>Peggy Lee Guest Star</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Guest Star #283: Peggy Lee (U.S. Defense Savings Bonds)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>U.S. Treasury</strong><br>1952-08-24<br>(Show #283)</td>\n<td><strong>U.S. Treasury</strong><br>U.S. Defense Bonds</td>\n<td><strong>Peggy Lee</strong>, <strong>The Dave Barbour Band</strong></td>\n<td><strong>U.S. Savings Bonds Division</strong>, <strong>Del Sharbutt</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Vocal&quot;, &quot;Easy Listening&quot;, &quot;Jazz&quot;, &quot;Morale&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Sultry jazz vocalist Peggy Lee headlines the Treasury Department&#39;s <em>Guest Star</em> program, performing mesmerizing renditions of &#39;You Go to My Head&#39; and &#39;Lover&#39; accompanied by guitarist Dave Barbour to promote U.S. Defense Bonds.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Guest_Star_1958_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Lauritz Melichor</code>, <code>Lauritz Melchior Guest Star</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Guest Star #596: Lauritz Melchior (U.S. Savings Bonds)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>U.S. Treasury</strong><br>1958-08-24<br>(Show #596)</td>\n<td><strong>U.S. Treasury</strong><br>U.S. Savings Bonds</td>\n<td><strong>Lauritz Melchior</strong> (Heldentenor), <strong>Ray Bloch Orchestra</strong></td>\n<td><strong>U.S. Savings Bonds Division</strong>, <strong>Del Sharbutt</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Classical&quot;, &quot;Vocal&quot;, &quot;Opera&quot;, &quot;Morale&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>World-renowned Wagnerian heldentenor Lauritz Melchior performs booming operatic selections and charming Danish folk ballads with Ray Bloch&#39;s Orchestra, urging Americans to invest in their nation&#39;s future through U.S. Savings Bonds.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Mystery_Theater_1948_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Death Weeping Bride</code>, <code>Inspector Hearthstone 1948</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Death and the Weeping Bride (Starring Alfred Shirley as Inspector Hearthstone — Molle)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1948-08-24<br>8:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sterling Drug Inc.</strong><br>Molle Shaving Cream</td>\n<td><strong>Alfred Shirley</strong> (Hearthstone), <strong>James Monks</strong> (Sam Cook)</td>\n<td><strong>Frank Wilson</strong> (Writer), <strong>Frank Telford</strong>, <strong>Frank Gallop</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Police&quot;, &quot;Procedural&quot;, &quot;British&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Scotland Yard&#39;s Inspector Hearthstone investigates the poisoning of a wealthy London aristocrat murdered at the reception altar of his lavish Mayfair wedding, uncovering a jealous plot disguised as a bride&#39;s curse.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Inner_Sanctum_1941_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Wail of Death</code>, <code>Boris Karloff Inner Sanctum</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Wail of Death (Starring Boris Karloff — Inner Sanctum Mystery)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Blue Network (WJZ)</strong><br>1941-08-24<br>8:30 PM EDST</td>\n<td><strong>Carter Products</strong><br>Carter&#39;s Little Liver Pills &amp; Arrid</td>\n<td><strong>Raymond Edward Johnson</strong> (Host), <strong>Boris Karloff</strong>, <strong>Santos Ortega</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Himan Brown</strong> (Creator/Director), <strong>Dwight Weist</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Horror&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Supernatural&quot;, &quot;Macabre&quot;, &quot;Thriller&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>As the squeaking door swings shut, host Raymond welcomes Boris Karloff in a macabre tale of an eccentric collector of cursed Irish artifacts who is stalked through a foggy London mansion by the shrieking phantom wail of a banshee.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 24</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 24</strong>: 30</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
