    "html": "<h2>August 24 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 01)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch initiates the <strong>August 24 Calendar Walk</strong>, documenting the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 24</strong> across American network broadcasting history (1939–1949):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 24 Archival Inventory (Increment 01)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Sea_Hound_1942_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Caribbean Convoy</code>, <code>Sea Hound CIAA 1942</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Captain Silver &amp; The Caribbean Convoy (The Sea Hound — CIAA Wartime Broadcast)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Blue Network (WJZ)</strong><br>1942-08-24<br>5:00 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Coordinator Inter-American Affairs</td>\n<td><strong>Bobby Hastings</strong> (Captain Silver), <strong>Kenneth Daigneau</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Frank Dahm</strong> (Writer), <strong>Cyril Armbrister</strong>, <strong>Doug Browning</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Juvenile&quot;, &quot;Nautical&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;War&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Master mariner Captain Silver sails the experimental schooner <em>Sea Hound</em> into Caribbean waters to outmaneuver an Axis U-boat wolfpack attempting to intercept a vital convoy of bauxite ore destined for Allied aircraft manufacturing.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Sea_Hound_1948_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Episode</code>, <code>Secret of Shark Reef</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Secret of Shark Reef (Starring Ken Daigneau as Captain Silver)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>ABC (WJZ)</strong><br>1948-08-24<br>5:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>ABC Youth Adventure</td>\n<td><strong>Ken Daigneau</strong> (Captain Silver), <strong>Bob Hastings</strong>, <strong>Alan Manson</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Frank Dahm</strong> (Writer), <strong>Cyril Armbrister</strong>, <strong>Doug Browning</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Juvenile&quot;, &quot;Nautical&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Captain Silver and the youthful crew of the <em>Sea Hound</em> brave a treacherous South American coral reef to rescue a marine biologist who discovered a submerged pre-Incan temple guarded by ruthless deep-sea salvagers.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Lone_Wolf_1948_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Shouldnt Happen Potato</code>, <code>Gerald Mohr Lone Wolf</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;It Shouldn&#39;t Happen to a Potato (Starring Gerald Mohr as The Lone Wolf)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1948-08-24<br>9:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Mutual Mystery Presentation</td>\n<td><strong>Gerald Mohr</strong> (Michael Lanyard), <strong>Charlotte Manson</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Louis Joseph Vance</strong>, <strong>Dwight Hauser</strong>, <strong>Dick Dudley</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Reformed jewel thief turned private investigator Michael Lanyard (The Lone Wolf) is hired by a panicked Idaho agricultural tycoon whose prize genetically engineered potato crop hides a smuggled shipment of uncut industrial diamonds.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Kay_Kyser_1939_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Were In The Money</code>, <code>Kay Kyser Lucky Strike</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Kollege of Musical Knowledge: We&#39;re in the Money (Lucky Strike)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Red (WEAF)</strong><br>1939-08-24<br>8:00 PM EDST</td>\n<td><strong>American Tobacco</strong><br>Lucky Strike Cigarettes</td>\n<td><strong>Kay Kyser</strong> (The Ol&#39; Professor), <strong>Ish Kabibble</strong>, <strong>Ginny Simms</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Bud Haggart</strong> (Writer), <strong>Kay Kyser</strong>, <strong>Verne Smith</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Quiz&quot;, &quot;Big Band&quot;, &quot;Swing&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Students, evenin&#39; folks, how y&#39;all?&quot; Kay Kyser dons cap and gown as the Ol&#39; Professor of Musical Knowledge, testing studio audience contestants on pop melodies, swinging to &#39;We&#39;re in the Money&#39;, and trading comedic barbs with Ish Kabibble for Lucky Strike.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Curtain_Time_1946_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Stolen Portrait</code>, <code>Curtain Time Milky Way</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Stolen Portrait (Starring Harry Elders &amp; Nanette Sargent — Mars Candy)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1946-08-24<br>7:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Mars, Incorporated</strong><br>Milky Way &amp; Snickers</td>\n<td><strong>Harry Elders</strong>, <strong>Nanette Sargent</strong>, <strong>Donald Gallagher</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Frank Higgins</strong> (Writer), <strong>Myron Golden</strong>, <strong>Charles Irving</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Anthology&quot;, &quot;Romance&quot;, &quot;Theater&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>From the Mars Candy playhouse, Harry Elders and Nanette Sargent star in a romantic comedy about an impoverished portrait artist whose masterpiece is mistakenly bought by a wealthy socialite at a charity auction.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Curtain_Time_1949_08_24.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Ring for the Teacher</code>, <code>Curtain Time Mars</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;A Ring for the Teacher (Starring Harry Elders &amp; Beryl Vaughn — Milky Way)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1949-08-24<br>10:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Mars, Incorporated</strong><br>Milky Way &amp; Forever Yours</td>\n<td><strong>Harry Elders</strong>, <strong>Beryl Vaughn</strong>, <strong>Arthur Peterson</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Frank Higgins</strong> (Writer), <strong>Myron Golden</strong>, <strong>Charles Irving</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Anthology&quot;, &quot;Romance&quot;, &quot;Theater&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>A heartwarming comedy about a shy small-town schoolteacher who receives an anonymous heirloom diamond engagement ring in the morning mail, setting off a town-wide matchmaking frenzy.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 24 (Walk 01)</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 24</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
