    "html": "<h2>August 23 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 59)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 23</strong> across American network and AFRS military broadcasting history (1943–1959):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 23 Archival Inventory (Increment 59)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Jubilee_1943_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>AFRS Jubilee 41</code>, <code>Rochester Lucky Millinder</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;AFRS Jubilee #41: Rochester, Lucky Millinder &amp; The Charioteers&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>AFRS Syndication</strong><br>1943-08-23<br>(Show #41)</td>\n<td><strong>U.S. War Dept</strong><br>Armed Forces Radio Service</td>\n<td><strong>Ernie &quot;Bubbles&quot; Whitman</strong> (MC), <strong>Eddie &quot;Rochester&quot; Anderson</strong>, <strong>Lucky Millinder</strong></td>\n<td><strong>AFRS Radio Unit</strong>, Recorded at NBC Hollywood</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Jazz&quot;, &quot;Swing&quot;, &quot;Vocal&quot;, &quot;African American&quot;, &quot;Morale&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Master of ceremonies Ernie &#39;Bubbles&#39; Whitman hosts an electric African-American musical showcase for wartime troops overseas, starring comedian Eddie &#39;Rochester&#39; Anderson, soaring harmonies by The Charioteers, and driving big band swing by Lucky Millinder&#39;s Orchestra.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Aldrich_1946_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Henrys Bicycle Repair</code>, <code>Henry Aldrich 1946</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Henry&#39;s Bicycle Repair Shop (Post&#39;s Grape-Nuts Flakes)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1946-08-23<br>8:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>General Foods</strong><br>Post&#39;s Grape-Nuts Flakes &amp; Jell-O</td>\n<td><strong>Dick Jones</strong> (Henry), <strong>Jackie Kelk</strong> (Homer), <strong>House Jameson</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Clifford Goldsmith</strong> (Creator), <strong>Day Tuttle</strong>, <strong>Harry von Zell</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Sitcom&quot;, &quot;Teen&quot;, &quot;Domestic&quot;, &quot;Family&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Hen-reee! Henry Aldrich!&quot; Teenager Henry Aldrich opens an ambitious bicycle repair shop in the Aldrich family garage, accidentally taking apart the town mayor&#39;s tandem bicycle without labeling the gears.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Thin_Man_1946_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>TCOT Lost Dinner</code>, <code>Les Tremayne Thin Man</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Case of the Lost Dinner (Starring Les Tremayne &amp; Claudia Morgan as The Thin Man)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1946-08-23<br>8:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>General Foods</strong><br>Post&#39;s 40% Bran Flakes &amp; Maxwell</td>\n<td><strong>Les Tremayne</strong> (Nick Charles), <strong>Claudia Morgan</strong> (Nora Charles)</td>\n<td><strong>Dashiell Hammett</strong> (Creator), <strong>Himan Brown</strong>, <strong>Ed Herlihy</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;, &quot;Sophisticated&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>High-society sleuths Nick and Nora Charles are invited to a lavish penthouse dinner party where the guest of honor is poisoned between the soup and salad courses, prompting Nick to interrogate the eccentric dinner guests while mixing martinis.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Archie_Andrews_1947_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Archies Jalopy Trouble</code>, <code>Archie Andrews Swift 1947</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Archie&#39;s Jalopy Trouble for the Country Club Dance (Swift&#39;s Franks)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1947-08-23<br>10:30 AM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Swift &amp; Company</strong><br>Swift&#39;s Premium Franks &amp; Prem</td>\n<td><strong>Bob Hastings</strong> (Archie), <strong>Harlan Stone Jr.</strong> (Jughead), <strong>Gloria Mann</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Bob Montana</strong> (Creator), <strong>Kenneth MacGregor</strong>, <strong>Kenneth Banghart</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Sitcom&quot;, &quot;Teen&quot;, &quot;Comic Strips&quot;, &quot;Family&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Riverdale high schooler Archie Andrews schemes with best pal Jughead to fix his beat-up jalopy in time to take Veronica Lodge to the country club summer dance, triggering a comical chain reaction of mechanical disasters.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Words_Live_By_1953_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Story of Joseph Part 8</code>, <code>Words We Live By 1953</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Words We Live By: Human Problems of the Joseph Story (Part 8)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1953-08-23<br>10:30 AM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>NBC &amp; Jewish Theological Seminary</td>\n<td><strong>Dr. Louis Finkelstein</strong>, <strong>Lyman Bryson</strong> (Moderator)</td>\n<td><strong>NBC Public Affairs</strong>, <strong>Peter Roberts</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Docudrama&quot;, &quot;Religious&quot;, &quot;Literature&quot;, &quot;Educational&quot;, &quot;Philosophical&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In part eight of the profound Biblical exploration of the Joseph narrative, scholars discuss the themes of reconciliation, forgiveness, and moral resilience when Joseph confronts his brothers in Egypt.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Legends_Bible_1959_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The Book of Judges</code>, <code>Alexander Scourby Bible</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Legends of the Bible: The Book of Judges (Narrated by Alexander Scourby)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1959-08-23<br>12:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>NBC &amp; Jewish Theological Seminary</td>\n<td><strong>Alexander Scourby</strong> (Narrator), <strong>Joseph Julian</strong>, <strong>Roger De Koven</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Peter Barry</strong> (Writer), <strong>Daniel Sutter</strong>, <strong>Mel Brandt</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Religious&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Anthology&quot;, &quot;Literature&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Actor Alexander Scourby narrates the dramatic Biblical chronicles of the Book of Judges, portraying the heroic leadership of Gideon and Deborah as they rally the tribes of Israel against oppression.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 23</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 23</strong>: 354</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
