    "html": "<h2>August 23 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 53)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 23</strong> across American network broadcasting history (1937–1954):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 23 Archival Inventory (Increment 53)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Twenty_Questions_1947_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Regina Resnick</code>, <code>Ronson Twenty Questions</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Twenty Questions: Guest Panelist Regina Resnik (Ronson Lighters)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1947-08-23<br>8:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Ronson Art Metal</strong><br>Ronson Pocket &amp; Table Lighters</td>\n<td><strong>Bill Slater</strong> (Host), <strong>Fred Van Deventer</strong>, <strong>Florence Rinard</strong>, <strong>Regina Resnik</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Van Deventer Family</strong> (Producers), <strong>Frank Waldecker</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Quiz&quot;, &quot;Game Show&quot;, &quot;Panel&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Metropolitan Opera soprano Regina Resnik joins regular panelists Fred Van Deventer, Florence Rinard, and Herb Polesie as they deduce mystery animal, vegetable, and mineral subjects within twenty yes-or-no questions for Ronson Lighters.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Twenty_Questions_1952_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Eloise McElhone</code>, <code>Wildroot Twenty Questions</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Twenty Questions: Guest Eloise McElhone (Wildroot Cream-Oil)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1952-08-23<br>8:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Wildroot Company</strong><br>Wildroot Cream-Oil Hair Tonic</td>\n<td><strong>Bill Slater</strong> (Host), <strong>Fred Van Deventer</strong>, <strong>Eloise McElhone</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Fred Van Deventer</strong> (Producer), <strong>Frank Waldecker</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Quiz&quot;, &quot;Game Show&quot;, &quot;Panel&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Radio and television personality Eloise McElhone joins the expert panel to unravel tricky clues about historical figures and everyday objects in fewer than twenty questions.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Lyn_Murray_1944_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Music by Lyn Murray</code>, <code>Squibb Lyn Murray 1944</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Music by Lyn Murray and his Orchestra &amp; Chorus (Squibb)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC)</strong><br>1944-08-23<br>6:15 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>E.R. Squibb &amp; Sons</strong><br>Squibb Dental Cream &amp; Vitamins</td>\n<td><strong>Lyn Murray Orchestra &amp; Chorus</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Lyn Murray</strong> (Conductor), <strong>Jimmy Wallington</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Easy Listening&quot;, &quot;Choral&quot;, &quot;Vocal&quot;, &quot;Big Band&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Maestro Lyn Murray conducts his acclaimed orchestra and choral ensemble in melodic wartime arrangements of American popular standards, folk ballads, and patriotic melodies for Squibb.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Airport_1950_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Final Hour</code>, <code>Emergency Landing Idlewild</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Final Hour: Emergency Landing at Idlewild (Starring Robert Sterling &amp; Raymond Burr)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>ABC (WJZ)</strong><br>1950-08-23<br>9:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>ABC Dramatic Presentation</td>\n<td><strong>Robert Sterling</strong> (Bill Davis), <strong>Raymond Burr</strong>, <strong>Lurene Tuttle</strong></td>\n<td><strong>George Bellak</strong> (Writer), <strong>William D. Hamilton</strong>, <strong>George Ansbro</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Aviation&quot;, &quot;Suspense&quot;, &quot;Docudrama&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Airport Director Bill Davis and his air traffic control tower crew coordinate an intense emergency night blind landing for a transatlantic airliner low on fuel with disabled landing gear over New York&#39;s Idlewild Airport.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Fibber_1937_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Super Hotel Service</code>, <code>Fibber McGee Johnsons Wax</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Super Hotel Service on Vacation (Johnson&#39;s Wax)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Red (WEAF)</strong><br>1937-08-23<br>9:00 PM EDST</td>\n<td><strong>S.C. Johnson &amp; Son</strong><br>Johnson&#39;s Wax &amp; Glo-Coat</td>\n<td><strong>Jim Jordan</strong> (Fibber), <strong>Marian Jordan</strong> (Molly), <strong>Bill Thompson</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Don Quinn</strong> (Writer), <strong>Cecil Underwood</strong>, <strong>Harlow Wilcox</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Sitcom&quot;, &quot;Domestic&quot;, &quot;Vaudeville&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>While traveling on their summer vacation tour, Fibber McGee drives Molly to distraction by demanding excessive, ridiculous accommodations from the frantic staff of an upscale resort hotel.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Fibber_1954_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Beekeepers Guide</code>, <code>Fibber McGee Prudential 1954</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Subscribing to the Beekeeper&#39;s Guide (Prudential Insurance)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1954-08-23<br>10:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Prudential Insurance</strong><br>Strength of Gibraltar</td>\n<td><strong>Jim Jordan</strong> (Fibber), <strong>Marian Jordan</strong> (Molly), <strong>Arthur Q. Bryan</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Phil Leslie</strong> (Writer), <strong>Max Hutto</strong>, <strong>Harlow Wilcox</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Sitcom&quot;, &quot;Domestic&quot;, &quot;Small Town&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>At 79 Wistful Vista, Fibber convinces himself that backyard beekeeping will yield a lucrative honey fortune after mistakenly subscribing to a five-year magazine contract for <em>The Beekeeper&#39;s Guide</em>.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 23</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 23</strong>: 318</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
