    "html": "<h2>August 23 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 51)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 23</strong> across American network and syndicated broadcasting history (1935–1959):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 23 Archival Inventory (Increment 51)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Beat_Band_1944_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Hildegarde Beat Band</code>, <code>Kix Hildegarde 1944</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Beat the Band: Musical Quiz with Hildegarde (Kix Cereal)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Red (WEAF)</strong><br>1944-08-23<br>8:30 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>General Mills</strong><br>Kix Cereal &amp; Softasilk</td>\n<td><strong>Hildegarde</strong> (Hostess), <strong>Harry Sosnik Orchestra</strong>, <strong>Kim Loo Sisters</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Jack Hurdle</strong> (Producer), <strong>Tom Reddy</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Quiz&quot;, &quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Game Show&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>The Incomparable Hildegarde hosts the fast-paced musical quiz show <em>Beat the Band</em>, challenging studio contestants to stump Harry Sosnik&#39;s orchestra with obscure musical requests while tossing out fifty-dollar silver dollar prizes and singing romantic standards.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Socony_1935_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>You Do Something To Me</code>, <code>Christopher Morley 1935</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Socony Sketchbook: Christopher Morley &amp; Johnny Green (Mobilgas &amp; Mobiloil)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC)</strong><br>1935-08-23<br>8:00 PM EDST</td>\n<td><strong>Socony-Vacuum</strong><br>Mobilgas &amp; Mobiloil</td>\n<td><strong>Christopher Morley</strong>, <strong>Johnny Green Orchestra</strong>, <strong>Virginia Verrill</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Arthur Pryor Jr.</strong> (Producer), <strong>Kenneth Roberts</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Variety&quot;, &quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Literature&quot;, &quot;Easy Listening&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Author Christopher Morley spins literary vignettes and philosophical essays between lush arrangements by Johnny Green&#39;s Orchestra and vocal interpretations of Cole Porter&#39;s &#39;You Do Something to Me&#39; by Virginia Verrill.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Amos_Andy_1959_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Music Hall 30th Anniversary</code>, <code>Amos Andy 1959</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Amos &#39;n&#39; Andy Music Hall: 30th Anniversary Special (Freeman Gosden &amp; Charles Correll)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1959-08-23<br>7:05 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>CBS Radio Retrospective</td>\n<td><strong>Freeman Gosden</strong> (Amos / Kingfish), <strong>Charles Correll</strong> (Andy)</td>\n<td><strong>Freeman Gosden &amp; Charles Correll</strong>, <strong>Del Sharbutt</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Retrospective&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Freeman Gosden and Charles Correll host a special 30th anniversary commemorative broadcast looking back on three decades of radio history, playing vintage 1929 recordings and sharing memories of early radio pioneer days.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Beulah_1948_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Episode</code>, <code>Beulah Dreft 1948</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Henderson Barbecue Pit (Starring Hattie McDaniel as Beulah — Dreft)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1948-08-23<br>7:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Procter &amp; Gamble</strong><br>Dreft &amp; Oxydol Detergent</td>\n<td><strong>Hattie McDaniel</strong> (Beulah), <strong>Hugh Studebaker</strong>, <strong>Ernest Whitman</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Arthur Phillips</strong> (Writer), <strong>Helen Mack</strong>, <strong>Marvin Miller</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Sitcom&quot;, &quot;Domestic&quot;, &quot;Family&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Housekeeper Beulah helps the Henderson family untangle a comical domestic crisis when Mr. Henderson&#39;s overzealous attempt to build a backyard barbecue pit collapses the neighbor&#39;s prize flower trellis.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>10_2_4_Time_1943_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Dr Pepper Sons Pioneers</code>, <code>10-2-4 Time 1943</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;10-2-4 Time: The Sons of the Pioneers (Dr Pepper Show #142)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Syndication</strong><br>1943-08-23<br>(Show #142)</td>\n<td><strong>Dr Pepper Co.</strong><br>Drink a Bite to Eat at 10, 2 &amp; 4</td>\n<td><strong>Sons of the Pioneers</strong> (Bob Nolan, Tim Spencer, Hugh Farr)</td>\n<td><strong>Dr Pepper Bottling Co.</strong>, <strong>Jack Lacy</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Country&quot;, &quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Vocal&quot;, &quot;Folk&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Western harmony masters The Sons of the Pioneers perform spirited cowboy ballads and western standards including &#39;Cool Water&#39; and &#39;Tumbleweeds&#39; in a refreshing 15-minute musical interlude for Dr Pepper.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>10_2_4_Time_1944_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Singing Sands Alamosa</code>, <code>Dr Pepper 1944</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Singing Sands of Alamosa: The Sons of the Pioneers (Dr Pepper Show #298)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Syndication</strong><br>1944-08-23<br>(Show #298)</td>\n<td><strong>Dr Pepper Co.</strong><br>Drink a Bite to Eat at 10, 2 &amp; 4</td>\n<td><strong>Sons of the Pioneers</strong> (Bob Nolan, Lloyd Perryman, Karl Farr)</td>\n<td><strong>Dr Pepper Bottling Co.</strong>, <strong>Jack Lacy</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Country&quot;, &quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Vocal&quot;, &quot;Folk&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>The Sons of the Pioneers open their western musical showcase with the evocative harmonies of &#39;The Singing Sands of Alamosa&#39;, blending fiddle solos and western yodeling for Dr Pepper.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 23</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 23</strong>: 306</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
