    "html": "<h2>August 23 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 32)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 23</strong> across American network and syndicated broadcasting history (1945–1947):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 23 Archival Inventory (Increment 32)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Raffles_1945_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Murder Signs Its Name</code>, <code>Horace Braham Raffles</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Murder Signs Its Name (Starring Horace Braham as A.J. Raffles)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC)</strong><br>1945-08-23<br>8:30 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>CBS Mystery Presentation</td>\n<td><strong>Horace Braham</strong> (A.J. Raffles), <strong>Berry Kroeger</strong> (Bunny Manders)</td>\n<td><strong>E.W. Hornung</strong> (Author), <strong>James Monks</strong>, <strong>John Dietz</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;British&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Gentleman safecracker A.J. Raffles and companion Bunny Manders find themselves framed for the murder of an art collector when the real killer leaves Raffles&#39; signature calling card monogram at the crime scene.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Tide_Show_1945_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Episode</code>, <code>Dick Haymes Helen Forrest Tide</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Tide Show: Dick Haymes &amp; Helen Forrest with Gordon Jenkins&#39; Orchestra&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (KNX)</strong><br>1945-08-23<br>8:00 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Procter &amp; Gamble</strong><br>Tide Detergent</td>\n<td><strong>Dick Haymes</strong>, <strong>Helen Forrest</strong>, <strong>Gordon Jenkins and his Orchestra</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Arthur Moore</strong> (Director), <strong>Frank Martin</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Vocal&quot;, &quot;Pop&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Baritone Dick Haymes and songstress Helen Forrest share the summer microphone for Tide detergent, performing romantic duets including &#39;It Had to Be You&#39; and &#39;I&#39;ll Buy That Dream&#39;, backed by Gordon Jenkins&#39; Orchestra.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Myrt_Marge_1946_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>OToole Testifies</code>, <code>Producer Murder Trial</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;O&#39;Toole and Mrs. Hunt Testify in the Producer&#39;s Murder Trial&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Syndication</strong><br>1946-08-23<br>(World Broadcasting)</td>\n<td><strong>Local Commercials</strong><br>Syndicated Advertisers</td>\n<td><strong>Myrtle Vail</strong> (Myrt), <strong>Donna Damerel</strong> (Marge), <strong>Ray Hedge</strong>, <strong>Vinton Hayworth</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Myrtle Vail</strong> (Creator), <strong>Matt Crowley</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Soap Opera&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Theatre&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In the dramatic courtroom inquiry into the theatrical producer&#39;s death, stage manager O&#39;Toole and wardrobe mistress Mrs. Hunt give surprise testimony that exposes an embezzler and clears chorus girl Marge.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Hawk_Larabee_1947_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Gold Dead Mans Creek</code>, <code>Elliott Lewis Somber Jones</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Gold of Dead Man&#39;s Creek (Starring Elliott Lewis as Hawk Larabee)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (KNX)</strong><br>1947-08-23<br>7:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>CBS Western Drama</td>\n<td><strong>Elliott Lewis</strong> (Hawk Larabee), <strong>Barton Yarborough</strong> (Somber Jones)</td>\n<td><strong>Kenneth Perkins</strong> (Writer), <strong>William N. Robson</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Texas rancher Hawk Larabee and his dry-witted partner Somber Jones help a terrified young homesteader protect her late father&#39;s gold claim from an unscrupulous frontier land baron and his hired gunmen.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Mercury_1946_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Two Stories</code>, <code>Apple Tree Welles Pabst</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Apple Tree (Directed &amp; Hosted by Orson Welles — Pabst Blue Ribbon)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC)</strong><br>1946-08-23<br>10:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Pabst Brewing Co.</strong><br>Pabst Blue Ribbon Beer</td>\n<td><strong>Orson Welles</strong>, <strong>Mercedes McCambridge</strong>, <strong>Dan Seymour</strong></td>\n<td><strong>John Galsworthy</strong> (Author), <strong>Orson Welles</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Anthology&quot;, &quot;Literature&quot;, &quot;Experimental&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Orson Welles presents a brilliant double-feature adaptation for Pabst Blue Ribbon, directing and starring in John Galsworthy&#39;s bittersweet lyrical romance <em>The Apple Tree</em> alongside a dramatic modern vignette.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Passport_Romance_1946_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Episode ++++</code>, <code>Victoria Cordova Antonini</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Passport to Romance: Alfredo Antonini with Victoria Cordova Singing Latin Classics&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1946-08-23<br>11:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>CBS Music Presentation</td>\n<td><strong>Alfredo Antonini and his Pan-American Orchestra</strong>, <strong>Victoria Cordova</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Alfredo Antonini</strong> (Conductor), <strong>Frank Gallop</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Latin&quot;, &quot;Vocal&quot;, &quot;Easy Listening&quot;, &quot;Romance&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Maestro Alfredo Antonini leads the Pan-American Orchestra in lush Latin American melodies and romantic continental waltzes, spotlighting vocalist Victoria Cordova singing &#39;Bésame Mucho&#39; and &#39;Estrellita&#39;.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 23</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 23</strong>: 192</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
