    "html": "<h2>August 23 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 30)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 23</strong> across American network and syndicated broadcasting history (1937–1956):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 23 Archival Inventory (Increment 30)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Screen_Guild_1943_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Skylark</code>, <code>Screen Guild Skylark 1943</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Skylark (Starring Claudette Colbert &amp; Ray Milland — Lady Esther)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (KNX)</strong><br>1943-08-23<br>10:00 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Lady Esther, Ltd.</strong><br>4-Purpose Face Cream &amp; Powder</td>\n<td><strong>Claudette Colbert</strong>, <strong>Ray Milland</strong>, <strong>Binnie Barnes</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Samson Raphaelson</strong> (Author), <strong>Bill Lawrence</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Romance&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Adaptation&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Claudette Colbert and Ray Milland star in Samson Raphaelson&#39;s sophisticated romantic comedy <em>Skylark</em>, playing a neglected advertising executive&#39;s wife who hires an eccentric bohemian lawyer to stage a pretend flirtation to win back her husband&#39;s romantic attention.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Bill_Lance_1947_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Episode</code>, <code>Counterfeit Heir Gerald Mohr</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Case of the Counterfeit Heir (Starring Gerald Mohr as Bill Lance)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>ABC (WJZ)</strong><br>1947-08-23<br>9:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>ABC Detective Drama</td>\n<td><strong>Gerald Mohr</strong> (Bill Lance), <strong>Howard McNear</strong>, <strong>Cathy Lewis</strong></td>\n<td><strong>J. Benton Cheney</strong> (Creator), <strong>James Fonda</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Globe-trotting private investigator Bill Lance and his eccentric valet Ulysses Higgins investigate a fraudulent claimant attempting to seize a deceased shipping magnate&#39;s estate, unmasking an international syndicate of identity thieves.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Cisco_Kid_1955_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Law of the Dead</code>, <code>Cisco Kid Jack Mather 1955</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Law of the Dead (Starring Jack Mather as The Cisco Kid)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual</strong><br>1955-08-23<br>5:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Wonder Bread</strong><br>Local Advertisers</td>\n<td><strong>Jack Mather</strong> (The Cisco Kid), <strong>Harry Lang</strong> (Pancho)</td>\n<td><strong>Jeanne Yount</strong> (Director), <strong>Michael Rye</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Children&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>The Cisco Kid and his loyal companion Pancho ride into a ghost town where an outlaw band uses spooky graveyard superstitions to frighten off prospectors while looting an abandoned silver mine.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Cisco_Kid_1956_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Stagecoach Gold Ambush</code>, <code>Jack Mather Mel Blanc</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Stagecoach Gold Ambush (Starring Jack Mather &amp; Mel Blanc)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual</strong><br>1956-08-23<br>5:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Weber&#39;s Bread</strong><br>Regional Advertisers</td>\n<td><strong>Jack Mather</strong> (The Cisco Kid), <strong>Mel Blanc</strong> (Pancho)</td>\n<td><strong>Jeanne Yount</strong> (Director), <strong>Michael Rye</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Children&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>The Cisco Kid and Pancho track a gang of masked road agents who ambushed the Butterfield Overland stagecoach, recovering a stolen bullion shipment and clearing an innocent young stablehand.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Jerry_Circus_1937_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Zeke Leaves Fast</code>, <code>Jerry Circus Ep 77</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Jerry of the Circus #77: Zeke Flees the Big Top (Kerr Mason Jars)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Syndication</strong><br>1937-08-23<br>(Transcribed Ep 77)</td>\n<td><strong>Kerr Glass Mfg.</strong><br>Kerr Mason Jars &amp; Fruit Caps</td>\n<td><strong>Tommy Cook</strong> (Jerry), <strong>Patrick J. Kelly</strong>, <strong>Earle Hodgins</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Master Radio Productions</strong>, <strong>Jimmy Wallington</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Children&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Circus&quot;, &quot;Family&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In Episode 77 of <em>Jerry of the Circus</em>, young Jerry and circus clown Bardo uncover suspicious financial sabotage in the big top accounting tent, causing crooked roustabout Zeke to flee the circus grounds ahead of the local sheriff.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Claudia_David_1948_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Summer Theatre</code>, <code>Claudia David Coca Cola</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;An Evening at the Summer Theatre (Coca-Cola)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1948-08-23<br>4:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>The Coca-Cola Co.</strong><br>Coca-Cola</td>\n<td><strong>Patricia Ryan</strong> (Claudia), <strong>Richard Kollmar</strong> (David)</td>\n<td><strong>Rose Franken</strong> (Author), <strong>Paul Stewart</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Romance&quot;, &quot;Domestic&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Young suburban couple Claudia and David Naughton attend an eccentric Connecticut summer stock playhouse production, where Claudia gets unexpectedly recruited to step into a leading dramatic role when the lead actress walks out.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 23</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 23</strong>: 180</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
