    "html": "<h2>August 23 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 23)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 23</strong> across American network broadcasting history (1939–1959):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 23 Archival Inventory (Increment 23)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Gabriel_Heatter_1944_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>New War in Europe</code>, <code>Paris Liberation Romania</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Gabriel Heatter: &#39;There&#39;s a New War in Europe Tonight&#39; (Kreml &amp; Forhan&#39;s)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1944-08-23<br>9:00 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Forhan&#39;s &amp; Kreml</strong><br>Forhan&#39;s Toothpaste &amp; Kreml Hair</td>\n<td><strong>Gabriel Heatter</strong> (News Analyst)</td>\n<td><strong>Mutual News Bureau</strong>, New York</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;News&quot;, &quot;War&quot;, &quot;Commentary&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Commentator Gabriel Heatter opens with his famous signature phrase, breaking electrifying wartime bulletins on the uprising of the French Resistance inside Paris and Romania&#39;s dramatic surrender and declaration of war against Nazi Germany.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Broadway_Beat_1952_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Dr Lyle Murder Case</code>, <code>Danny Clover Midtown Clinic</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Dr. Lyle Murder Case (Starring Larry Thor as Danny Clover)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1952-08-23<br>8:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>CBS Radio Noir</td>\n<td><strong>Larry Thor</strong> (Danny Clover), <strong>Charles Calvert</strong>, <strong>Jack Kruschen</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Morton Fine &amp; David Friedkin</strong> (Writers), <strong>Elliott Lewis</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Noir&quot;, &quot;Police&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Detective Danny Clover walks the neon-lit pavement of Times Square to investigate the fatal shooting of a society doctor in his Midtown examination clinic, uncovering an illicit prescription racket tied to an off-Broadway nightclub singer.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Coke_Time_1954_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Make Love To Me</code>, <code>Eddie Fisher Coca Cola</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Coke Time with Eddie Fisher: &#39;Make Love to Me&#39; (Coca-Cola)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual &amp; NBC</strong><br>1954-08-23<br>8:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>The Coca-Cola Co.</strong><br>Coca-Cola</td>\n<td><strong>Eddie Fisher</strong>, <strong>Axel Stordahl and his Orchestra</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Herb Moss</strong> (Director), <strong>Fred Robbins</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Vocal&quot;, &quot;Pop&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Pop singing sensation Eddie Fisher performs live for Coca-Cola, serenading listeners with his smash hit arrangement of &#39;Make Love to Me&#39; alongside romantic standards accompanied by Axel Stordahl and his Orchestra.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Radio_News_1939_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Martin Dies HUAC</code>, <code>Nazi-Soviet Pact Reaction Dies</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Rep. Martin Dies: On the Hitler-Stalin Non-Aggression Pact &amp; Un-American Activities&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Red (WEAF)</strong><br>1939-08-23<br>7:30 PM EDST</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>NBC Public Affairs Special</td>\n<td><strong>Rep. Martin Dies Jr.</strong> (Chairman, HUAC)</td>\n<td><strong>NBC News Bureau</strong>, Washington</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;News&quot;, &quot;Politics&quot;, &quot;Public Affairs&quot;, &quot;Speech&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>House Un-American Activities Committee Chairman Martin Dies delivers a nationwide radio address in response to the newly signed Hitler-Stalin Non-Aggression Pact, declaring that Nazi fascism and Soviet communism have merged into a unified threat against American democratic institutions.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Gunsmoke_1959_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The Reed Survives</code>, <code>Matt Dillon Dodge City</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Reed Survives (Starring William Conrad as Matt Dillon)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (KNX)</strong><br>1959-08-23<br>6:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Participating Advertisers</td>\n<td><strong>William Conrad</strong> (Matt Dillon), <strong>Parley Baer</strong>, <strong>Howard McNear</strong>, <strong>Georgia Ellis</strong></td>\n<td><strong>John Meston &amp; Norman Macdonnell</strong> (Creators), <strong>Les Crutchfield</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>United States Marshal Matt Dillon steps in when an arrogant, hot-headed young gunslinger rides into Dodge City determined to provoke a deadly showdown with an aging, peaceful homesteader who refuses to be drawn into gun violence.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Grand_Slam_1949_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Episode</code>, <code>Irene Beasley Wonder Bread</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Grand Slam Musical Quiz with Irene Beasley (Wonder Bread)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1949-08-23<br>11:30 AM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Continental Baking</strong><br>Wonder Bread &amp; Hostess Cupcakes</td>\n<td><strong>Irene Beasley</strong> (Hostess), <strong>Dwight Weist</strong>, <strong>Bob Hannon</strong>, <strong>Jesse Crawford</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Irene Beasley</strong> (Creator), <strong>Herb Moss</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Game Show&quot;, &quot;Quiz&quot;, &quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Hostess Irene Beasley challenges radio listeners and studio contestants with musical trivia clues and bridge-themed five-question rounds to win the Grand Slam jackpot of U.S. Savings Bonds and kitchen appliances for Wonder Bread.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 23</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 23</strong>: 138</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
