    "html": "<h2>August 23 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 22)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 23</strong> across American broadcasting history (1939–1950):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 23 Archival Inventory (Increment 22)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Mr_Malone_1947_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Case Poisoned Uncle</code>, <code>Frank Lovejoy Mr Malone</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Case of the Poisoned Uncle (Starring Frank Lovejoy as John J. Malone)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>ABC (WJZ)</strong><br>1947-08-23<br>9:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>ABC Mystery Drama</td>\n<td><strong>Frank Lovejoy</strong> (John J. Malone), <strong>Joan Alexander</strong> (Maggie), <strong>Berry Kroeger</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Craig Rice</strong> (Creator), <strong>Gene Wang</strong> (Writer), <strong>William Spier</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Chicago criminal defense lawyer John J. Malone takes the case of a wealthy socialite accused of poisoning her uncle, using unorthodox courtroom theatrics and streetwise interrogation at Joe the Angel&#39;s bar to trap the real beneficiary.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Fantasy_1947_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Fantasy (Audition)</code>, <code>Entity from the Void Pilot</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Fantasy (Audition Pilot): &#39;Entity from the Void&#39; (Starring John McIntire &amp; William Conrad)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Hollywood</strong><br>1947-08-23<br>(Audition Disc)</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>NBC Audition Series</td>\n<td><strong>John McIntire</strong> (Narrator), <strong>William Conrad</strong>, <strong>Jeanette Nolan</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Arch Oboler &amp; Ray Bradbury</strong> (Writers), <strong>Homer Fickett</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Science Fiction&quot;, &quot;Horror&quot;, &quot;Anthology&quot;, &quot;Speculative&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In this audition pilot for the speculative radio anthology <em>Fantasy</em>, narrator John McIntire dramatizes the chilling story of an astronomer who discovers an invisible cosmic consciousness drifting into Earth&#39;s upper atmosphere to drain human mental willpower.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>WWII_News_1939_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Nazi Bolshevism Soviet Fascism</code>, <code>Dorothy Thompson Pact</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Dorothy Thompson: On the Nazi-Soviet Non-Aggression Pact (Molotov-Ribbentrop)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Blue (WJZ)</strong><br>1939-08-23<br>10:30 PM EDST</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>NBC News Analysis</td>\n<td><strong>Dorothy Thompson</strong> (Commentator &amp; Political Analyst)</td>\n<td><strong>NBC News Bureau</strong>, New York</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;News&quot;, &quot;History&quot;, &quot;War&quot;, &quot;Commentary&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Renowned political commentator Dorothy Thompson delivers an urgent news analysis of the shocking non-aggression pact signed in Moscow between Nazi Germany and the Soviet Union, warning American listeners that Hitler and Stalin&#39;s alliance makes immediate European war inevitable.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Damon_Runyon_1949_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>So You Wont Talk</code>, <code>Broadway Silent Safecracker</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;So You Won&#39;t Talk (Starring John Brown as &#39;Broadway&#39;)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mayfair Syndication</strong><br>1949-08-23<br>(KFI / Syndicated)</td>\n<td><strong>Local Commercials</strong><br>Co-op Advertisers</td>\n<td><strong>John Brown</strong> (Broadway), <strong>Alan Reed</strong>, <strong>Sheldon Leonard</strong>, <strong>Lurene Tuttle</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Damon Runyon</strong> (Author), <strong>Russell Hughes</strong> (Adapter), <strong>Richard Sanville</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;, &quot;Anthology&quot;, &quot;Broadway&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Broadway narrator John Brown relates the humorous tale of an obstinate safecracker who refuses to speak a single word following a bank job, driving police detectives and underworld loan sharks crazy until a chorus girl coaxes the combination out of him.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Mr_DA_1944_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Intimidated Jury</code>, <code>Mr Stanleys Jury Fixed</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Case of the Intimidated Jury (Vitalis Hair Tonic)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WEAF)</strong><br>1944-08-23<br>9:30 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Bristol-Myers Co.</strong><br>Vitalis Hair Tonic &amp; Sal Hepatica</td>\n<td><strong>Jay Jostyn</strong> (Paul Garrett), <strong>Vicki Vola</strong> (Miss Miller), <strong>Len Doyle</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Phillips H. Lord</strong> (Creator), <strong>Edward Byron</strong> (Director), <strong>Fred Cole</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Police&quot;, &quot;Procedural&quot;, &quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Mr. District Attorney Paul Garrett and investigator Harrington intervene in a high-stakes racketeering trial after a syndicate boss threatens the families of jurors, planting an undercover detective inside the jury sequester hotel to catch the bribe-paying bagman.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Mr_DA_1950_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Pebble of Death</code>, <code>Slingshot Curare Assassin</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Case of the Pebble of Death (Vitalis &amp; Ipana)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1950-08-23<br>9:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Bristol-Myers Co.</strong><br>Vitalis Hair Tonic &amp; Ipana</td>\n<td><strong>Jay Jostyn</strong> (Paul Garrett), <strong>Vicki Vola</strong> (Miss Miller), <strong>Len Doyle</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Robert J. Shaw</strong> (Writer), <strong>Edward Byron</strong> (Director), <strong>Fred Cole</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Police&quot;, &quot;Procedural&quot;, &quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>District Attorney Paul Garrett hunts a bizarre serial assassin who assassinates prominent diamond merchants using an untraceable custom slingshot loaded with heavy industrial ball-bearing &#39;pebbles&#39; coated in rare South American curare poison.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 23</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 23</strong>: 132</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
