    "html": "<h2>August 23 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 17)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, serial multi-part narrative arcs, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 23</strong> across American and British broadcasting history (1938–1988):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 23 Archival Inventory (Increment 17)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Superman_1945_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The Flood - Part 13</code>, <code>Metropolis Dam Disaster</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Flood (Part 13) — The Metropolis Dam Disaster (Kellogg&#39;s Pep)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1945-08-23<br>5:15 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Kellogg Company</strong><br>Kellogg&#39;s Pep Cereal</td>\n<td><strong>Bud Collyer</strong> (Superman), <strong>Joan Alexander</strong> (Lois), <strong>Jackie Kelk</strong></td>\n<td><strong>B.P. Freeman</strong> (Writer), <strong>George Lowther</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Superhero&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Disaster&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In Part 13 of <em>The Flood</em>, a torrential cloudburst ruptures the mountain reservoir above Metropolis, prompting Superman to fly at superhuman velocity to brace the crumbling concrete wall with granite boulders and save trapped valley villagers.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Superman_1946_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Candy Meyers Big Story 2</code>, <code>Extortion Gang Notebook</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Candy Meyer&#39;s Big Story (Part 2 of 8) — The Extortion Notebook&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1946-08-23<br>5:15 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Kellogg Company</strong><br>Kellogg&#39;s Pep Cereal</td>\n<td><strong>Bud Collyer</strong> (Superman), <strong>Ronald Liss</strong> (Candy Meyer), <strong>Jackie Kelk</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Robert &amp; Jessica Maxwell</strong> (Writers), <strong>Jackson Beck</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Superhero&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Children&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In Part 2 of <em>Candy Meyer&#39;s Big Story</em>, teenage copy boy Candy Meyer stumbles across a coded notebook belonging to an extortion gang while running errands for the <em>Daily Planet</em>, escaping into a crowded subway station before the gangsters corner him.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Superman_1948_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Mystery Of The Letter 6</code>, <code>Stolen Chemical Formula</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Mystery of the Letter (Part 6 of 11) — The Stolen Chemical Formula&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1948-08-23<br>5:15 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Mutual Radio Drama</td>\n<td><strong>Bud Collyer</strong> (Superman), <strong>Joan Alexander</strong> (Lois), <strong>Julian Noa</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Jessica Maxwell</strong> (Director), <strong>Jackson Beck</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Superhero&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In Part 6 of <em>The Mystery of the Letter</em>, Lois Lane is abducted by a criminal syndicate demanding the return of a stolen industrial chemical formula, prompting Superman to follow the kidnappers&#39; tire tracks across state lines to a remote farmhouse hideout.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Superman_1950_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Curse of Devils Creek</code>, <code>Devils Creek Outlaws</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Curse of Devil&#39;s Creek (Starring Michael Fitzmaurice)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>ABC (WJZ)</strong><br>1950-08-23<br>5:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>ABC Youth Drama</td>\n<td><strong>Michael Fitzmaurice</strong> (Superman), <strong>Joan Alexander</strong> (Lois), <strong>Jack Grimes</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Allen Ducovny</strong> (Director), <strong>Ross Martin</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Superhero&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Clark Kent and Jimmy Olsen travel to the ghost town of Devil&#39;s Creek to investigate rumors of a gold mine curse, discovering that an armed outlaw gang used trick mirrors and smoke to frighten away homesteaders while extracting high-grade ore.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Tinker_Tailor_1988_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Episode 4</code>, <code>George Smiley Connie Sachs</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Tinker, Tailor, Soldier, Spy (Part 4 of 7) — George Smiley Interrogates Connie Sachs&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>BBC Radio 4</strong><br>1988-08-23<br>3:00 PM</td>\n<td><strong>Non-commercial</strong><br>BBC Public Service</td>\n<td><strong>Bernard Hepton</strong> (George Smiley), <strong>Michael Jayston</strong>, <strong>Frank Windsor</strong></td>\n<td><strong>John le Carré</strong> (Author), <strong>René Basilico</strong> (Adapter), <strong>John Tydeman</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Spy&quot;, &quot;Espionage&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Cold War&quot;, &quot;British&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In Part 4 of the definitive BBC serialization of John le Carré&#39;s espionage masterpiece, retired spymaster George Smiley interviews ailing former Circus researcher Connie Sachs, unearthing critical files that confirm a high-level Soviet mole codenamed &#39;Gerald&#39; operates within the British Secret Service.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Camel_Caravan_1938_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Love Me Or Leave Me</code>, <code>Benny Goodman Martha Tilton</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Camel Caravan: Benny Goodman with Martha Tilton Singing &#39;Love Me or Leave Me&#39;&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC)</strong><br>1938-08-23<br>9:30 PM EDST</td>\n<td><strong>R.J. Reynolds Tobacco Co.</strong><br>Camel Cigarettes &amp; Prince Albert</td>\n<td><strong>Benny Goodman</strong>, <strong>Martha Tilton</strong>, <strong>Teddy Wilson</strong>, <strong>Gene Krupa</strong>, <strong>Lionel Hampton</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Harry Ackerman</strong> (Director), <strong>Dan Seymour</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Big Band&quot;, &quot;Swing&quot;, &quot;Jazz&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>The King of Swing Benny Goodman and his Orchestra perform live for Camel Cigarettes, featuring vocal sensation Martha Tilton singing &#39;Love Me or Leave Me&#39; alongside dazzling swing improvisations from the Benny Goodman Quartet on &#39;Stompin&#39; at the Savoy&#39;.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 23</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 23</strong>: 102</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
