    "html": "<h2>August 23 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 16)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, serial multi-part narrative arcs, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 23</strong> across American and British broadcasting history (1940–2010):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 23 Archival Inventory (Increment 16)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Ray_Bradbury_2010_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Tomorrows Child 2010</code>, <code>Bradbury 90th Birthday</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Tomorrow&#39;s Child (Ray Bradbury 90th Birthday Special)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>PRI / BYU Radio</strong><br>2010-08-23<br>(Birthday Special)</td>\n<td><strong>Non-commercial</strong><br>Corporation for Public Broadcasting</td>\n<td><strong>Ray Bradbury</strong> (Birthday Intro), <strong>Paul Frees</strong>, <strong>Ron Frederickson</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mike McDonough</strong> (Adapter &amp; Producer), BYU Radio</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Science Fiction&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Speculative&quot;, &quot;Anthology&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In a special 90th birthday broadcast honoring Ray Bradbury, the author introduces the dramatic adaptation of <em>Tomorrow&#39;s Child</em>, exploring the emotional struggle of parents whose newborn infant is born into an incomprehensible fourth dimension.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Son_Of_Cliche_1983_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Public Parks Dedication</code>, <code>Grant Naylor Series 1 Ep 1</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Son of Cliché (Series 1, Episode 1) — Rob Grant &amp; Doug Naylor&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>BBC Radio 4</strong><br>1983-08-23<br>10:30 PM</td>\n<td><strong>Non-commercial</strong><br>BBC Public Service</td>\n<td><strong>Chris Barrie</strong>, <strong>Nick Maloney</strong>, <strong>Nick Wilton</strong>, <strong>Amanda Swift</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Rob Grant &amp; Doug Naylor</strong> (Writers), <strong>Mike Craig</strong> (Producer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Satire&quot;, &quot;Sketch&quot;, &quot;Parody&quot;, &quot;British&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Future <em>Red Dwarf</em> creators Rob Grant and Doug Naylor launch their groundbreaking sketch comedy series, lampooning bureaucratic council ceremonies with a disastrous public park dedication and featuring Chris Barrie&#39;s razor-sharp vocal impressions.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Kingsmen_1949_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The Dorothy Kirsten</code>, <code>Kingsmen Darby Kirsten</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Kingsmen Quartet with Special Guest Dorothy Kirsten&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1949-08-23<br>7:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>NBC Music Presentation</td>\n<td><strong>The Kingsmen Quartet</strong> (Ken Darby), <strong>Dorothy Kirsten</strong> (Soprano)</td>\n<td><strong>Ken Darby</strong> (Music Director), <strong>Frank Gallop</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Vocal&quot;, &quot;Barbershop&quot;, &quot;Easy Listening&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Ken Darby and The Kingsmen vocal quartet harmonize with Metropolitan Opera soprano Dorothy Kirsten, performing Broadway show tunes and traditional Americana ballads including &#39;Summertime&#39; and &#39;Stars in My Eyes&#39;.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Superman_1940_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Mayan Treasure 6 of 6</code>, <code>Superman Mayan Lava Climax</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Mayan Treasure (Part 6 of 6) — The Fiery Lava Climax&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1940-08-23<br>5:15 PM EDST</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Mutual Youth Serial</td>\n<td><strong>Bud Collyer</strong> (Superman), <strong>Joan Alexander</strong> (Lois), <strong>Julian Noa</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Siegel &amp; Shuster</strong> (Creators), <strong>George Lowther</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Superhero&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Children&quot;, &quot;Serial&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In Part 6 and the thrilling serial climax of <em>The Mayan Treasure</em>, Superman flies deep into the crumbling subterranean ruins of a Yucatan pyramid to rescue Lois Lane and Professor Henderson from a fiery underground lava trap, capturing the treasure-hunting bandits.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Superman_1943_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Civil Air Patrol 4</code>, <code>Superman Kelloggs Pep 1943</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Civil Air Patrol (Part 4) — Kellogg&#39;s Pep Cereal&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1943-08-23<br>5:15 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Kellogg Company</strong><br>Kellogg&#39;s Pep Cereal</td>\n<td><strong>Bud Collyer</strong> (Superman), <strong>Jackie Kelk</strong> (Jimmy Olsen), <strong>Julian Noa</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Robert &amp; Jessica Maxwell</strong> (Writers), <strong>Jackson Beck</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Superhero&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;War&quot;, &quot;Serial&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In Part 4 of <em>The Civil Air Patrol</em>, Clark Kent and cub reporter Jimmy Olsen investigate suspected enemy saboteurs signaling Axis submarines off the Atlantic coast, flying with the youth patrol as Superman intercepts a rogue seaplane.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Superman_1944_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Ghosts of the Air 7</code>, <code>Superman Invisible Plane</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Ghosts of the Air (Part 7) — The Invisible Plane (Kellogg&#39;s Pep)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1944-08-23<br>5:15 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Kellogg Company</strong><br>Kellogg&#39;s Pep Cereal</td>\n<td><strong>Bud Collyer</strong> (Superman), <strong>Joan Alexander</strong> (Lois), <strong>Jackie Kelk</strong></td>\n<td><strong>B.P. Freeman</strong> (Writer), <strong>George Lowther</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Superhero&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Science Fiction&quot;, &quot;Serial&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In Part 7 of <em>Ghosts of the Air</em>, Superman battles an invisible high-altitude aircraft piloted by an international criminal syndicate that has been vanishing commercial passenger planes mid-flight over the Midwest.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 23</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 23</strong>: 96</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
