    "html": "<h2>August 23 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 11)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 23</strong> across American, British, and Canadian broadcasting history (1946–1998):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 23 Archival Inventory (Increment 11)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Adventures_Of_Maisie_1946_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Episode</code>, <code>Maisie Mountain Resort</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Maisie at the Mountain Resort (Eversharp Schick Injector)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC)</strong><br>1946-08-23<br>8:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>The Eversharp Co.</strong><br>Eversharp Schick Injector</td>\n<td><strong>Ann Sothern</strong> (Maisie), <strong>Elliott Lewis</strong>, <strong>Hans Conried</strong>, <strong>Elvia Allman</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Arthur Phillips</strong> (Writer), <strong>Tony Martin</strong> (Director), <strong>John Conte</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Sitcom&quot;, &quot;Romance&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Good-hearted Brooklyn showgirl Maisie Ravier takes a job as a social hostess at an eccentric mountain resort, trying to mediate a bitter feud between two wealthy hotel guests while evading a persistent phony French count.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>A_Life_In_Your_Hands_1949_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Contested Will</code>, <code>Jonathan Kincaid Kool</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Case of the Contested Will (Kool Cigarettes)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1949-08-23<br>8:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Brown &amp; Williamson</strong><br>Kool Cigarettes</td>\n<td><strong>Carlton KaDell</strong> (Jonathan Kincaid), <strong>Myron McCormick</strong>, <strong>Joan Banks</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Erle Stanley Gardner</strong> (Creator), <strong>Chick Vincent</strong> (Director), <strong>Bud Collyer</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Legal&quot;, &quot;Courtroom&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Defense attorney Jonathan Kincaid cross-examines a scheming nephew who accuses a family nurse of poisoning a wealthy dowager, proving in open court that the nephew forged a second will using an outdated notary stamp.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Mystery_Project_1997_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Dog It Was That Died</code>, <code>Tom Stoppard CBC</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Dog It Was That Died (by Tom Stoppard)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBC Radio</strong><br>1997-08-23<br>6:30 PM</td>\n<td><strong>Non-commercial</strong><br>Canadian Broadcasting Corp.</td>\n<td><strong>Kenneth Welsh</strong> (George), <strong>Fiona Reid</strong> (Penelope), <strong>Douglas Campbell</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Tom Stoppard</strong> (Writer), <strong>James Roy</strong> (Producer &amp; Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Satire&quot;, &quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Spy&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Canadian&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Kenneth Welsh and Fiona Reid star in Tom Stoppard&#39;s espionage comedy about a deeply conflicted Cold War double agent who loses his sanity trying to remember which intelligence service he is actually loyal to.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Strange_Seeker_1998_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The Dobsky Engine</code>, <code>Perpetual Motion Mystery</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Dobsky Engine (The Perpetual Motion Mystery)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>BBC Radio 4</strong><br>1998-08-23<br>9:00 PM</td>\n<td><strong>Non-commercial</strong><br>BBC Public Service</td>\n<td><strong>John Rowe</strong> (The Seeker / Narrator), <strong>Geoffrey Whitehead</strong>, <strong>Janet Maw</strong></td>\n<td><strong>John Peacock</strong> (Writer), <strong>Cherry Cookson</strong> (Producer &amp; Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;British&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>An antiquarian investigator researches the Victorian disappearance of an eccentric inventor who claimed to have constructed a perpetual motion steam engine, tracing his hidden blueprints to a bricked-up cellar in Yorkshire.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Barrie_Craig_1953_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Dig Another Grave</code>, <code>Gravedigger Blackmail</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Dig Another Grave (Starring William Gargan)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1953-08-23<br>10:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>NBC Crime Drama</td>\n<td><strong>William Gargan</strong> (Barrie Craig), <strong>Ralph Bell</strong>, <strong>Santos Ortega</strong></td>\n<td><strong>John Roeburt</strong> (Writer), <strong>Himan Brown</strong> (Director), <strong>Don Pardo</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Noir&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Hardboiled Madison Avenue private eye Barrie Craig is hired by a frantic socialite whose supposedly deceased first husband is blackmailing her from the shadows, unearthing an empty grave in a storm-drenched cemetery.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Under_Arrest_1953_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Waterfront Hijackers</code>, <code>Captain Drake Under Arrest</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Waterfront Cargo Hijackers (Captain John Drake)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1953-08-23<br>5:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Mutual Radio Series</td>\n<td><strong>Joe DeSantis</strong> (Captain Drake), <strong>Mandel Kramer</strong>, <strong>Bryna Raeburn</strong></td>\n<td><strong>William Sweets</strong> (Writer), <strong>Wynn Wright</strong> (Director), <strong>Carl Warren</strong></td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Police&quot;, &quot;Procedural&quot;, &quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;True Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Police Captain John Drake breaks up an armed waterfront hijacking ring that has been intercepting transatlantic cargo shipments, going undercover on the docks to trap the fence in a warehouse sting.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 23</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 23</strong>: 66</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
