    "html": "<h2>August 23 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment (Increment 07)</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, serial multi-part narrative structures, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 23</strong> across American network, syndication, and public broadcasting history (1947–1992):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 23 Archival Inventory (Increment 07)</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Gangbusters_1947_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Masquerade Bandit</code>, <code>Tydol Gangbusters 1947</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Case of the Masquerade Bandit (Tydol Gasoline)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>ABC (WJZ)</strong><br>1947-08-23<br>9:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Tide Water Oil</strong><br>Tydol Gasoline &amp; Veedol Oil</td>\n<td><strong>Col. H. Norman Schwarzkopf</strong> (Host), <strong>Ken Lynch</strong>, <strong>Don MacLaughlin</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Phillips H. Lord</strong> (Creator &amp; Director), <strong>Roger Krupp</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;True Crime&quot;, &quot;Police&quot;, &quot;Procedural&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Colonel H. Norman Schwarzkopf presents the true case of a cunning bank robber who donned elaborate theatrical makeup and disguises to hold up armored payroll couriers across Ohio, evading local posses until state troopers traced his custom latex adhesives.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Gangbusters_1952_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Rheuark Williams Dyer</code>, <code>Four State Safe Crackers</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Case of Rheuark, Williams, Dyer, and Eaton (The Safe-Cracking Gang)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1952-08-23<br>9:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>CBS Radio Crime Drama</td>\n<td><strong>John Larkin</strong> (Narrator), <strong>Lawson Zerbe</strong>, <strong>Mandel Kramer</strong>, <strong>Frank Lovejoy</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Phillips H. Lord</strong> (Director), <strong>Art Hannes</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;True Crime&quot;, &quot;Police&quot;, &quot;Procedural&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Police detectives and FBI agents track a heavily armed quartet of escaped convicts and professional safe-crackers across four southern states, cornering the gang in a shootout at a rural mountain hideout.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Gangbusters_1954_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Charlestown Siege</code>, <code>Boston Prison Breakout</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Case of the Charlestown State Prison Siege&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1954-08-23<br>8:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Mutual Radio Series</td>\n<td><strong>Bill Smith</strong> (Narrator), <strong>Larry Haines</strong>, <strong>Bob Dryden</strong>, <strong>Ralph Bell</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Phillips H. Lord</strong> (Creator), <strong>Leonard Valenta</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;True Crime&quot;, &quot;Police&quot;, &quot;Procedural&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>A dramatization of the armed standoff at the historic Massachusetts State Prison in Charlestown, where four desperate inmates took prison guards hostage in the maximum-security wing, leading to a seventy-two-hour siege resolved by state police negotiators.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Police_Blotter_1957_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Midnight Jewelry Heist</code>, <code>Desk Sergeant Log</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Police Blotter: The Midnight Skylight Jewelry Heist&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual Syndication</strong><br>1957-08-23<br>(Radio Vignette)</td>\n<td><strong>Local Advertisers</strong><br>Commercial Co-op</td>\n<td><strong>Sgt. Frank Reynolds</strong> (Desk Sergeant)</td>\n<td><strong>Mutual Radio Features</strong>, New York</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;True Crime&quot;, &quot;Police&quot;, &quot;Short&quot;, &quot;Documentary&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>The police desk sergeant reviews the midnight patrol logs, recounting how a rookie beat officer caught an armed burglar escaping through a jewelry store skylight after hearing the burglar trip a silent seismic alarm.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Chet_Chetter_1992_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>1-800-BigBang Part 2</code>, <code>Tales from Morgue Serial</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;1-800-BigBang (Part 2) — The Cosmic Telephone Hotline&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NPR / ZBS Syndication</strong><br>1992-08-23<br>(ZBS Foundation)</td>\n<td><strong>CPB / ZBS</strong><br>Corporation for Public Broadcasting</td>\n<td><strong>Peter Coyote</strong> (Chet Chetter), <strong>Meat Loaf</strong>, <strong>Kirby Morrow</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Meat Loaf &amp; Thomas Lopez</strong> (Writers &amp; Directors), <strong>Bob Bielecki</strong> (Sound)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Satire&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Serial&quot;, &quot;Surrealism&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In Part 2 of the surreal mystery serial <em>1-800-BigBang</em>, sardonic coroner Chet Chetter investigates a bizarre hotline that connects callers directly to catastrophic cosmic explosions, teaming with an eccentric demolition expert to trace the telephone switchboard before the universe implodes.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Frank_Merriwell_1947_08_23.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Secret of Mesa</code>, <code>Red Rock Mesa Gold Mine</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Secret of the Red Rock Mesa&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WNBC)</strong><br>1947-08-23<br>10:00 AM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>NBC Youth Drama</td>\n<td><strong>Lawson Zerbe</strong> (Frank Merriwell), <strong>Jean Gillespie</strong>, <strong>Harold Studer</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Gilbert Patten</strong> (Creator), <strong>Ruth Adams Knight</strong> (Writer), <strong>Joe King</strong> (Director)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Children&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Sports&quot;, &quot;Serial&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>All-American Yale athlete and adventurer Frank Merriwell and sweetheart Inza Burrage travel into the New Mexico desert to investigate mysterious ghost sightings atop an ancient red rock mesa, exposing a team of unscrupulous prospectors mining stolen uranium ore.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 23</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 23</strong>: 42</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
