    "html": "<h2>August 22 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for 6 historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 22</strong> across American, Australian, and British broadcasting history (1944–1998):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 22 Exhaustive Archival Inventory</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Bing_Crosby_1961_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>First Song - Rain</code>, <code>Bing and Rosie Rain</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Bing Crosby &amp; Rosemary Clooney Sing &#39;Rain&#39; with The Buddy Cole Trio&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1961-08-22<br>10:45 AM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Daytime CBS Network</td>\n<td><strong>Bing Crosby</strong>, <strong>Rosemary Clooney</strong>, <strong>Buddy Cole and his Trio</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Bill Morrow</strong> (Writer), <strong>Murdo MacKenzie</strong> (Director), <strong>Ken Carpenter</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;, &quot;Easy Listening&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Bing Crosby and Rosemary Clooney delight daytime radio audiences with effortless close-harmony banter and duets, opening with their upbeat rendition of &#39;Rain&#39; alongside Buddy Cole&#39;s swinging organ and piano accompaniment.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Louisiana_Hayride_1959_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Linda Brannon Hayride</code>, <code>Lonesome When You&#39;re Gone</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Linda Brannon: &#39;I&#39;ll Be Lonesome When You&#39;re Gone&#39; (Live at Shreveport Auditorium)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>KWKH Shreveport</strong><br>1959-08-22<br>8:00 PM CST</td>\n<td><strong>Southern Maid Donuts</strong><br>&amp; Johnny Fair Syrup</td>\n<td><strong>Frank Page</strong> (MC), <strong>Linda Brannon</strong>, <strong>The Four B&#39;s</strong>, <strong>Jimmy Martin</strong>, <strong>Hayride Band</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Horace Logan</strong> (Producer), <strong>Bob Sullivan</strong> (Sound Engineer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Country&quot;, &quot;Rockabilly&quot;, &quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Live Remote&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Master of Ceremonies Frank Page presents live country and rockabilly performances from the Shreveport Municipal Memorial Auditorium, featuring teenage sensation Linda Brannon singing her breakout rockabilly hit &#39;I&#39;ll Be Lonesome When You&#39;re Gone&#39;.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Bob_Barkley_1951_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Shanghai Explosion</code>, <code>Bund Waterfront Sabotage</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Shanghai Explosion (The Bund Waterfront Sabotage)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Grace Gibson Syndication</strong><br>1951-08-22<br>(2UW Sydney)</td>\n<td><strong>Regional Advertisers</strong><br>Australian Syndication</td>\n<td><strong>Bruce Stewart</strong> (Bob Barkley), <strong>Lyndall Barbour</strong>, <strong>John Tate</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Ross Higgins</strong> (Writer), <strong>Grace Gibson Productions</strong> Sydney</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Espionage&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Thriller&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Undercover operative Bob Barkley navigates the dangerous neon-lit back alleys and docks of post-war Shanghai, racing to disarm a timed explosives cache planted aboard an Allied munitions freighter docked along the Bund.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Dick_Barton_1998_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Atom Formula Formula</code>, <code>Dick Barton AU</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Secret of the Atom Formula&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>ABC Radio National</strong><br>1998-08-22<br>(Australia)</td>\n<td><strong>Non-commercial</strong><br>Australian Broadcasting Corp.</td>\n<td><strong>Peter Collingwood</strong> (Dick Barton), <strong>Gordon Glenwright</strong> (Snowey), <strong>Ronald Morse</strong> (Jock)</td>\n<td><strong>Edward J. Mason</strong> (Creator), <strong>Rodney Wylie</strong> (Director), <em>Devil&#39;s Galop</em> Theme</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Spy&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Ex-commando and special agent Captain Dick Barton and loyal companions Jock Anderson and Snowey White pursue a ruthless international syndicate across the Scottish Highlands to recover stolen blueprints for a top-secret atomic rocket guidance system.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Nick_Carter_1944_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Twilight Terror Part 2</code>, <code>Kem-Tone Carter 1944</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Twilight Terror (Part 2)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1944-08-22<br>8:30 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Acme White Lead</strong><br>Kem-Tone &amp; Lin-X Clear Gloss</td>\n<td><strong>Lon Clark</strong> (Nick Carter), <strong>Charlotte Manson</strong> (Patsy Bowen), <strong>Ed Latimer</strong> (Brennan)</td>\n<td><strong>Ferrin Fraser</strong> (Writer), <strong>Jock MacGregor</strong> (Director), <strong>Michael Fitzmaurice</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>In Part 2 of a suspenseful two-part investigation, master detective Nick Carter and assistant Patsy Bowen enter the catacombs beneath a secluded coastal estate to trap a masked murderer who uses hallucinogenic gases to drive wealthy heirs insane.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Nick_Carter_1954_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Lovelorn Corpse</code>, <code>Lonely Hearts Poisoner</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Case of the Lovelorn Corpse&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1954-08-22<br>4:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Mutual Mystery Series</td>\n<td><strong>Lon Clark</strong> (Nick Carter), <strong>Charlotte Manson</strong> (Patsy Bowen), <strong>Ed Latimer</strong> (Brennan)</td>\n<td><strong>Ferrin Fraser</strong> (Writer), <strong>Jock MacGregor</strong> (Director), <strong>John Sylvester</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Hardboiled&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Nick Carter and Patsy Bowen investigate the cyanide poisoning of an elderly bachelor at a seaside hotel, uncovering a fraudulent matrimonial agency that targeted lonely bachelors to collect fraudulent life insurance policies.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 22</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 22</strong>: 188</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
