    "html": "<h2>August 22 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for 6 historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 22</strong> across American and South African broadcasting history (1932–1975):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 22 Exhaustive Archival Inventory</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>The_Saint_1945_08_22_GI.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The G.I. Ghouls</code>, <code>Black Market Penicillin</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The G.I. Ghouls (War Surplus Smugglers)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (KNX)</strong><br>1945-08-22<br>8:00 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Campbell Soup Co.</strong><br>Campbell&#39;s Soups &amp; V8</td>\n<td><strong>Brian Aherne</strong> (Simon Templar), <strong>Louise Arthur</strong> (Patricia Holm), <strong>Ken Christy</strong> (Inspector Fernack)</td>\n<td><strong>Leslie Charteris</strong> (Creator), <strong>Louis Vittes</strong> (Writer), <strong>Helen Mack</strong> (Director), <strong>Dick Joy</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Simon Templar uncovers a ruthless post-war black market ring hijacking army surplus penicillin and surgical equipment from military warehouses, cornering the gang&#39;s corrupt quartermaster in an abandoned airfield hangar.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Jello_1932_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Carnival Night</code>, <code>Canada Dry 17</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Jack and Mary at the Summer Carnival&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Blue (WJZ)</strong><br>1932-08-22<br>8:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Canada Dry Ginger Ale</strong><br>&quot;The Champagne of Ginger Ales&quot;</td>\n<td><strong>Jack Benny</strong>, <strong>Mary Livingstone</strong>, <strong>George Olsen and his Music</strong>, <strong>Ethel Shutta</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Harry Conn</strong> (Writer), <strong>Alois Havrilla</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Variety&quot;, &quot;Music&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Jack Benny takes Mary Livingstone to a summer traveling carnival, getting into a hilarious feud with a carnival barker at the ring-toss booth after spending two dollars trying to win a cheap plaster kewpie doll.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Serenade_Blue_1954_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>They Can&#39;t Take That Away</code>, <code>USAF Band 402</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;USAF Band &amp; Singing Sergeants: &#39;They Can&#39;t Take That Away From Me&#39;&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>USAF Transcription</strong><br>1954-08-22<br>(Bolling AFB)</td>\n<td><strong>Non-commercial</strong><br>USAF Recruiting Service</td>\n<td><strong>USAF Band &amp; Singing Sergeants</strong>, <strong>Col. George S. Howard</strong>, <strong>Bobby Nichols</strong></td>\n<td><strong>USAF Radio Branch</strong>, Bolling Air Force Base Washington</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Music&quot;, &quot;Big Band&quot;, &quot;Military&quot;, &quot;Easy Listening&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Colonel George S. Howard directs The United States Air Force Band and The Singing Sergeants in patriotic and swing arrangements, opening with &#39;They Can&#39;t Take That Away From Me&#39; and &#39;I&#39;ve Got the World on a String&#39; for Air Force recruiting.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Perry_Mason_1951_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Forged Holographic Will</code>, <code>Della Street Discovery</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Case of the Forged Holographic Will&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WCBS)</strong><br>1951-08-22<br>2:15 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Procter &amp; Gamble</strong><br>Tide (&quot;Tide&#39;s in, dirt&#39;s out&quot;) &amp; Camay</td>\n<td><strong>John Larkin</strong> (Perry Mason), <strong>Joan Alexander</strong> (Della Street), <strong>Matt Crowley</strong> (Paul Drake), <strong>Mandel Kramer</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Erle Stanley Gardner</strong> (Creator), <strong>Dan Shuffman</strong> (Writer), <strong>Bob Dixon</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Legal&quot;, &quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Serial&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Defense attorney Perry Mason and Della Street uncover erased pencil notations on a contested holographic will, proving that an unscrupulous probate executor altered the inheritance terms to disinherit the testator&#39;s young daughter.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Authors_Studio_1975_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The Homestead</code>, <code>Karoo Short Story</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Homestead in the Karoo&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>SABC English Service</strong><br>1975-08-22<br>(Durban / Jo&#39;burg)</td>\n<td><strong>Non-commercial</strong><br>SABC Cultural Programming</td>\n<td><strong>Michael Coulson</strong> (Host), <strong>SABC Drama Repertory Company</strong></td>\n<td><strong>SABC Drama Department</strong>, Durban/Johannesburg Studios</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Literature&quot;, &quot;Anthology&quot;, &quot;Cultural&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>A dramatized literary adaptation presenting a gripping South African short story about an isolated Karoo sheep farmer whose family confronts an encroaching drought and the mysterious arrival of a wounded trekker seeking shelter.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Proudly_We_Hail_1948_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The Fairway Acres</code>, <code>Brian Donlevy Veterans</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Fairway Acres (Starring Brian Donlevy)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>U.S. Military Syndication</strong><br>1948-08-22<br>(Disc 42)</td>\n<td><strong>U.S. Armed Forces</strong><br>Army &amp; Air Force Recruiting</td>\n<td><strong>Brian Donlevy</strong> (Tom Gallagher), <strong>Frances Rafferty</strong> (Ellen)</td>\n<td><strong>Charles Schenck</strong> (Director), <strong>Vladimir Selinsky</strong> (Music), <strong>Kenneth Banghart</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Military&quot;, &quot;Anthology&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Hollywood star Brian Donlevy headlines the story of a decorated World War II veteran who designs a cooperative suburban housing community for returning soldiers, fighting off corrupt municipal zoning commissioners to see the development completed.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 22</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 22</strong>: 134</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
