    "html": "<h2>August 22 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, commercial sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for 6 historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 22</strong> across American and British broadcasting history (1932–1961):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 22 Exhaustive Archival Inventory</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Performers</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Ma_Perkins_1949_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Fay&#39;s Decision</code>, <code>Rushville Lumberyard 4112</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Fay&#39;s Difficult Decision at the Lumberyard&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC / WBBM)</strong><br>1949-08-22<br>1:15 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Procter &amp; Gamble</strong><br>Oxydol Laundry Detergent</td>\n<td><strong>Virginia Payne</strong> (Ma Perkins), <strong>Charles Egelston</strong> (Shuffle Shober), <strong>Rita Ascot</strong> (Fay), <strong>Murray Forbes</strong> (Willie)</td>\n<td><strong>Frank &amp; Anne Hummert</strong> (Producers), <strong>George Fogle</strong> (Director), <strong>Jack Brinkley</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Soap Opera&quot;, &quot;Serial&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Ma Perkins and her trusted lumberyard partner Shuffle Shober comfort Fay as she wrestles with a life-changing career decision in Rushville, offering wise homespun counsel on family loyalty and integrity.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Ma_Perkins_1950_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Evy&#39;s New House Plans</code>, <code>Rushville Blueprints 4372</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Evy&#39;s House Construction Blueprints&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC)</strong><br>1950-08-22<br>1:15 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Procter &amp; Gamble</strong><br>Oxydol &amp; Dreft Detergents</td>\n<td><strong>Virginia Payne</strong> (Ma Perkins), <strong>Charles Egelston</strong> (Shuffle Shober), <strong>Kay Campbell</strong> (Evy), <strong>Murray Forbes</strong> (Willie)</td>\n<td><strong>Frank &amp; Anne Hummert</strong>, <strong>Philip Bowman</strong> (Director), <strong>Jack Brinkley</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Soap Opera&quot;, &quot;Serial&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Evy Fitz brings contractor blueprints to the Rushville lumberyard office, seeking Ma&#39;s approval on mortgage estimates while Shuffle warns Willie about inflated building supply costs.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Ceiling_Unlimited_1943_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Air Transport Command</code>, <code>Hump Airlift Supply</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Air Transport Command Over the Hump (Narrated by Joseph Cotten)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (KNX / WABC)</strong><br>1943-08-22<br>2:00 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Lockheed Vega</strong><br>Aircraft Corporation (&quot;Look to Lockheed&quot;)</td>\n<td><strong>Joseph Cotten</strong> (Host / Narrator), supporting Hollywood dramatic cast</td>\n<td><strong>Frank Wilson</strong> (Writer), <strong>Paul Stewart</strong> (Director), <strong>Wilbur Hatch</strong> (Music)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Documentary&quot;, &quot;Aviation&quot;, &quot;War&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Joseph Cotten narrates the harrowing story of U.S. Army Air Transport Command pilots flying unarmed Douglas C-47 Skytrain cargo planes over the Himalayan &#39;Hump&#39; to deliver aviation fuel and ammunition to Allied airfields in China.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Dick_Tracy_1947_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Waterfront Refinery Ambush</code>, <code>Dick Tracy Quaker 214</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Waterfront Refinery Ambush&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>ABC (WJZ)</strong><br>1947-08-22<br>5:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>The Quaker Oats Co.</strong><br>Puffed Wheat &amp; Puffed Rice (&quot;Shot from guns!&quot;)</td>\n<td><strong>Matt Crowley</strong> (Dick Tracy), <strong>Howard Smith</strong> (Pat Patton), <strong>Jackie Kelk</strong> (Junior), <strong>Helen Lewis</strong> (Tess)</td>\n<td><strong>Chester Gould</strong> (Creator), <strong>Sidney Slon</strong> (Writer), <strong>Dan Seymour</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Children&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Two-way wrist radio crackling with static, detective Dick Tracy and junior partner Pat Patton pursue a jewel-smuggling syndicate into an abandoned waterfront sugar refinery, springing a trap on the gang&#39;s trigger-happy enforcer.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Whack_O_1961_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>The Dismissal</code>, <code>Chiselbury School Inquiry</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Dismissal&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>BBC Light Programme</strong><br>1961-08-22<br>8:00 PM BST</td>\n<td><strong>Non-commercial</strong><br>BBC Light Entertainment</td>\n<td><strong>Jimmy Edwards</strong> (Prof. James Edwards), <strong>Arthur Howard</strong> (Mr. Pettigrew), <strong>Kenneth Cope</strong> (Inspector), <strong>Edwin Apps</strong> (Lumley)</td>\n<td><strong>Frank Muir &amp; Denis Norden</strong> (Writers), <strong>Charles Maxwell</strong> (Producer), Aeolian Hall London</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Sitcom&quot;, &quot;British&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Disreputable, cane-swishing headmaster Professor Jimmy Edwards faces immediate dismissal when the Board of Governors and a strict School Inspector arrive unannounced to investigate missing school funds at Chiselbury Public School.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Death_Valley_Days_1932_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>A Parsnip Stew</code>, <code>Prospector&#39;s Last Meal</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;A Parsnip Stew&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC Blue (WJZ)</strong><br>1932-08-22<br>8:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Pacific Coast Borax Co.</strong><br>20 Mule Team Borax &amp; Boraxo</td>\n<td><strong>Tim Frawley</strong> (The Old Ranger), <strong>Jack MacBryde</strong> (Grizzly Pete), <strong>John White</strong> (Lonesome Cowboy)</td>\n<td><strong>Ruth Cornwall Woodman</strong> (Writer), <strong>Felix Mills</strong> (Organist), <strong>George Hicks</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Anthology&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>The Old Ranger recounts the humorous frontier tale of a snowbound Nevada gold prospector who guards a single pot of boiling parsnip stew against ravenous camp claim jumpers during the blizzard of 1888.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 22</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 22</strong>: 104</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
