    "html": "<h2>August 22 Exhaustive Archival Metadata Enrichment</h2>\n<p>This archival dispatch documents the comprehensive provenance, broadcast scheduling, sponsorship, credited cast, production personnel, alternate circulating titles, and story synopses for 6 historical broadcasts transmitting on <strong>August 22</strong> across American and British broadcasting history (1940–1950):</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>August 22 Exhaustive Archival Inventory</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename &amp; Alternate Titles</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Network, Airdate &amp; Showtime</th>\n<th>Sponsor &amp; Commercial Ads</th>\n<th>Credited Cast &amp; Characters</th>\n<th>Director, Writers &amp; Crew</th>\n<th>Genres</th>\n<th>Story-First Plot Synopsis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Date_Judy_1945_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Judy&#39;s Triple Date</code>, <code>Country Club Dance</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Great Country Club Dance Rivalry&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NBC (WEAF)</strong><br>1945-08-22<br>8:30 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Bristol-Myers Company</strong><br>Ipana Toothpaste &amp; Sal Hepatica Laxative</td>\n<td><strong>Louise Erickson</strong> (Judy Foster), <strong>John Brown</strong> (Melvyn Foster), <strong>Lois Corbett</strong> (Dora Foster), <strong>Dix Davis</strong> (Oogie Pringle), <strong>Sandra Gould</strong> (Mitzi)</td>\n<td><strong>Jerome Lawrence &amp; Robert E. Lee</strong> (Writers/Directors), <strong>Buzz Adlam</strong> (Orchestra), <strong>Ken Niles</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Comedy&quot;, &quot;Teen&quot;, &quot;Family&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Judy Foster accidentally accepts invitations to the end-of-summer country club dance from three different boys at once, forcing her father Melvyn and boyfriend Oogie Pringle into frantic maneuvers to juggle the arrivals at the front door.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Famous_Jury_Trials_1944_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Hartwell Embezzlement Trial</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The People vs. Richard Hartwell&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Blue / ABC (WJZ)</strong><br>1944-08-22<br>9:00 PM EWT</td>\n<td><strong>Williamson Candy Co.</strong><br>Oh Henry! Candy Bars</td>\n<td><strong>Maurice Franklin</strong> (The Judge), <strong>Donald Buka</strong> (Richard Hartwell), <strong>Raymond Edward Johnson</strong> (Prosecutor), <strong>Bill Johnstone</strong> (Defense)</td>\n<td><strong>Clark Andrews</strong> (Director), <strong>Ray Erlenborn</strong> (Sound Effects), <strong>Roger Krupp</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Drama&quot;, &quot;Crime&quot;, &quot;Legal&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>The trial of bank teller Richard Hartwell, indicted for grand larceny and manslaughter following a fatal crash, where defense cross-examinations dissect ledger discrepancies to expose the branch manager as the mastermind.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>BBC_News_1940_08_22_Dover.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Convoy Shelled In Straits Of Dover</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;BBC News: Merchant Convoy Shelled in the Straits of Dover&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>BBC Home Service</strong><br>1940-08-22<br>9:00 PM BST</td>\n<td><strong>Non-commercial</strong><br>Ministry of Information / BBC</td>\n<td><strong>Frank Phillips &amp; Joseph Macleod</strong> (Newsreaders), <strong>Robin Duff</strong> (War Correspondent)</td>\n<td><strong>BBC News Division</strong> (Production), Broadcasting House London</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;News&quot;, &quot;Historical&quot;, &quot;Documentary&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>News bulletin reporting on the heavy cross-Channel artillery duel between German coastal batteries at Cap Gris-Nez and British artillery at Dover, documenting an Allied merchant convoy surviving dive-bomber assaults and heavy shelling in the Straits of Dover during the Battle of Britain.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Mystery_Week_1946_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>COT Golden Fleece Murders 4</code>, <code>Lone Wolf 4</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Case of the Golden Fleece Murders: Part 4&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>CBS (WABC)</strong><br>1946-08-22<br>5:00 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Procter &amp; Gamble</strong><br>Ivory Snow &amp; Crisco Shortening</td>\n<td><strong>Gerald Mohr</strong> (Michael Lanyard / The Lone Wolf), <strong>Mandel Kramer</strong> (Inspector Crane), <strong>Charlotte Manson</strong> (Elena Vance)</td>\n<td><strong>Bill Sweets</strong> (Director), <strong>Louis Joseph Vance</strong> (Original Author), <strong>Charles Paul</strong> (Organist), <strong>Fred Collins</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Mystery&quot;, &quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Michael Lanyard traces bloodstained Peruvian shipping manifests to a waterfront warehouse, discovering that raw fleece bales were used to smuggle stolen Inca gold artifacts and identifying the purser&#39;s murderer before the ship departs.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Champion_1949_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>Lost Treasure Part 1</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Mystery of the Lost Treasure: Chapter 1&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Syndicated</strong><br>1949-08-22<br>(Flying A)</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining / Regional</strong><br>Flying A Productions</td>\n<td><strong>Ricky Kelman</strong> (Ricky North), <strong>Champion</strong> (Wonder Horse), <strong>Jim Bannon</strong> (Sheriff Sandy North), <strong>Kenne Duncan</strong> (Blackie)</td>\n<td><strong>Louis Gray</strong> (Director), <strong>Carl Cotner</strong> (Music Director), <strong>Gene Autry</strong> (Executive Producer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Western&quot;, &quot;Adventure&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>While exploring an abandoned adobe mission bell tower, young Ricky North discovers an 18th-century Spanish treasure map; when two armed claim-jumpers ambush Ricky to seize it, Champion breaks his tether to fight off the outlaws and carry Ricky to safety.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Official_Det_1950_08_22.mp3</code> <br><em>Alt</em>: <code>When A Lady Turns To Crime</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;When a Lady Turns to Crime&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Mutual (WOR)</strong><br>1950-08-22<br>8:30 PM EDT</td>\n<td><strong>Sustaining</strong><br>Official Detective Stories Magazine</td>\n<td><strong>Craig McDonnell</strong> (Lt. Dan Britt), <strong>Doug Parkhirst</strong> (Sgt. Miller), <strong>Eleanor Audley</strong> (Victoria Van Horn)</td>\n<td><strong>Wynn Wright</strong> (Director), <strong>William Sweets</strong> (Script), <strong>Al Hogan</strong> (Sound Effects), <strong>Carl Warren</strong> (Announcer)</td>\n<td><code>[&quot;Crime&quot;, &quot;Detective&quot;, &quot;Drama&quot;]</code></td>\n<td>Lieutenant Dan Britt investigates the daylight armed robbery of a textile mill payroll truck, matching tire treads and rare French perfume at the crime scene to high-society matriarch Victoria Van Horn, who secretly bankrolled an interstate robbery gang.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Archival Verification Summary</em></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Target Calendar Day</strong>: August 22</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts Resolved This Increment</strong>: 6</li>\n<li><strong>Cumulative Resolved on August 22</strong>: 50</li>\n<li><strong>Target Repositories Synchronized</strong>: <code>radioindex.org-meta</code> and <code>radioindex.org-blog</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
