    "markdown": "# Archival Dispatch: 15 Master Broadcasts Dated Across Radio City Playhouse, The Bickersons, and Jackie Robinson\n\n**Date**: 2026-08-21  \n**Author**: radio index  \n**Tags**: Radio City Playhouse, The Bickersons, Don Ameche, Frances Langford, Jackie Robinson, NBC Radio, Original Filenames\n\n---\n\n## Batch 14 Forensic Discoveries\n\nBatch 14 resolves 15 landmark radio broadcasts across three classic properties: Harry W. Junkin's acclaimed NBC dramatic anthology ***Radio City Playhouse*** (1948–1949 master attraction runs), Philip Rapp's legendary comedy series ***The Bickersons*** (starring Don Ameche, Frances Langford, and Danny Thomas), and rare 1959 syndicated sports interviews hosted by baseball Hall of Famer ***Jackie Robinson***.\n\n---\n\n## 1. *Radio City Playhouse* — NBC Dramatic Anthology Attractions Dated\n\nDirected and produced by Harry W. Junkin from NBC Radio City in New York:\n\n| Original Circulating Filename | Canonical Title | Verified Airdate | Production Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `Radio_City_Playhouse_The_Promise.mp3` | **\"Attraction 14: The Promise\"** | **1948-10-04** | Written and directed by Harry W. Junkin; starring Bob Warren. |\n| `Radio_City_Playhouse_Strange_Identity.mp3` | **\"Attraction 21: Strange Identity\"** | **1948-11-22** | Psychological mystery drama written and directed by Harry W. Junkin. |\n| `Radio_City_Playhouse_Portrait_Of_Lenore.mp3` | **\"Attraction 23: Portrait of Lenore\"** | **1948-12-06** | Gothic radio thriller with special opening director address. |\n| `Radio_City_Playhouse_Legend_Of_Teresa.mp3` | **\"Attraction 44: The Legend of Teresa\"** | **1949-05-16** | Legendary radio performance introduced by announcer Fred Collins. |\n| `Radio_City_Playhouse_Birthday_Party.mp3` | **\"Attraction 48: The Birthday Party\"** | **1949-06-13** | Premier broadcast of a new dramatic script by guest author. |\n| `Radio_City_Playhouse_Level_Crossing.mp3` | **\"Attraction 50: Level Crossing\"** | **1949-06-27** | High-tension suspense thriller set at a remote railway crossing. |\n| `Radio_City_Playhouse_Look_What_Happened.mp3` | **\"Attraction 52: Look What Happened to Eddie\"** | **1949-07-11** | Hardboiled crime drama adapted for the summer NBC season. |\n| `Radio_City_Playhouse_Long_Distance.mp3` | **\"Attraction 57: Long Distance\"** | **1949-08-15** | Acclaimed solo telephone suspense play adapted for radio. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. *The Bickersons* — Don Ameche & Frances Langford NBC Comedy Classics\n\nPhilip Rapp's masterpiece of marital sparring, featuring Danny Thomas as Brother Amos:\n\n| Original Circulating Filename | Canonical Title | Verified Airdate | Comedy Sketch Details |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `Bickersons_Breakfast_Wants_Maid.mp3` | **\"Breakfast: Blanche Wants a Maid\"** | **1947-01-19** | Blanche demands a housekeeper while John complains about the dirty dishes. |\n| `Bickersons_The_Will.mp3` | **\"The Will (The Honeymoon Is Over)\"** | **1947-02-09** | John and Blanche argue over inheritance terms at 2:00 AM. |\n| `Bickersons_The_New_Tux.mp3` | **\"The New Tuxedo\"** | **1947-03-02** | Formal dinner preparations derail when John's tuxedo goes missing. |\n| `Bickersons_8th_Anniversary.mp3` | **\"8th Wedding Anniversary\"** | **1947-04-13** | Blanche expects diamonds while John offers sarcastic anniversary greetings. |\n| `Bickersons_Lose_Apartment.mp3` | **\"John's Insomnia / The Apartment Notice\"** | **1947-05-18** | John's late-night snoring leads to a noise dispute with the landlord. |\n\n---\n\n## 3. *Jackie Robinson's Radio Sports Show* (1959 Syndication)\n\n| Original Circulating Filename | Canonical Title | Verified Airdate | Interview Subject |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `Jackie_Robinson_Tom_Dorwin.mp3` | **\"Jackie Robinson Radio Show: Tom Dorwin (Water Ski Champion)\"** | **1959-07-15** | Jackie Robinson interviews the international water ski champion on boating safety. |\n| `Jackie_Robinson_Ted_Raynor.mp3` | **\"Jackie Robinson Radio Show: Ted Raynor (Sports Producer)\"** | **1959-07-20** | Jackie Robinson interviews TV producer Ted Raynor on championship bowling. |\n"
